1
00:01:37,001 --> 00:01:39,125
Madam, the auspicious time has arrived.

2
00:01:39,126 --> 00:01:40,251
Please bring the bride.

3
00:02:08,667 --> 00:02:09,417
Nivi...

4
00:02:10,417 --> 00:02:11,459
Ajay isn't coming.

5
00:02:12,209 --> 00:02:13,167
He doesn't want this marriage.

6
00:02:17,876 --> 00:02:22,209
He sent me here personally, saying,
'Uncle, please tell Nivi this on my behalf.'

7
00:02:29,626 --> 00:02:31,501
He has already left for Bangalore.

8
00:02:32,126 --> 00:02:33,251
His train leaves in a little while.

9
00:02:55,751 --> 00:02:56,292
So...

10
00:02:58,626 --> 00:02:59,334
it's our last day.

11
00:03:00,959 --> 00:03:03,209
From tomorrow, you'll be in Chennai,

12
00:03:03,751 --> 00:03:04,667
and I'll be in Bangalore.

13
00:03:05,501 --> 00:03:07,251
As long as we aren't afraid of drifting apart...

14
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:11,251
the physical distance doesn't matter.

15
00:03:19,126 --> 00:03:20,001
What's wrong?

16
00:03:22,334 --> 00:03:24,792
Are you worried that we still
haven't settled down yet?

17
00:03:25,292 --> 00:03:26,876
Should I talk to my parents?

18
00:03:27,542 --> 00:03:31,334
Don't worry about the long-distance
thing not working out, Ajay.

19
00:03:32,167 --> 00:03:33,917
Should I just move to Bangalore?

20
00:03:34,209 --> 00:03:36,751
I don't mind even if it takes me
a while to find a job there...

21
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:39,416
I really want to be...

22
00:03:39,417 --> 00:03:40,209
Her name is Jyo.

23
00:03:49,876 --> 00:03:50,584
She's a colleague.

24
00:03:51,251 --> 00:03:53,167
She supports me a lot at work.

25
00:03:54,084 --> 00:03:56,459
I don't know why,
but... I've started liking her.

26
00:03:57,376 --> 00:03:59,667
I haven't even told her yet.

27
00:04:00,542 --> 00:04:02,542
Honestly, I don't even know
when this feeling started.

28
00:04:03,501 --> 00:04:06,334
But I don't want to marry you while I'm still
this confused and end up cheating you, Nivi.

29
00:04:07,459 --> 00:04:08,042
I'm sorry.

30
00:04:08,876 --> 00:04:10,209
What are you saying, Ajay?

31
00:04:12,459 --> 00:04:13,459
Three years of love...

32
00:04:15,626 --> 00:04:18,084
we dreamt of so much together...

33
00:04:20,292 --> 00:04:24,042
We always said that even if we were the only
two people left in the world, we'd live happily.

34
00:04:24,876 --> 00:04:28,209
How many times did we say we'd
never get bored of each other?

35
00:04:31,709 --> 00:04:36,876
I can't even imagine anyone else by
my side but you, Ajay.

36
00:04:37,251 --> 00:04:37,709
Nivi...

37
00:04:40,876 --> 00:04:41,376
Ajay...

38
00:04:42,876 --> 00:04:44,917
this is just confusion, that's all!

39
00:04:46,251 --> 00:04:47,167
I can understand.

40
00:04:47,751 --> 00:04:49,876
Everyone goes through this phase in life.

41
00:04:50,751 --> 00:04:51,791
We can sort this out.

42
00:04:51,792 --> 00:04:53,417
Please, let's just sit down and talk.

43
00:04:57,084 --> 00:04:57,834
It's time.

44
00:04:58,709 --> 00:04:59,501
I have to go.

45
00:05:11,667 --> 00:05:12,209
I'm sorry.

46
00:05:12,459 --> 00:05:13,334
Please take care.

47
00:05:25,209 --> 00:05:25,876
Auntie...

48
00:05:26,001 --> 00:05:27,376
What's done is done.

49
00:05:27,709 --> 00:05:29,792
If she stays here,
she'll just slip deeper into depression.

50
00:05:30,084 --> 00:05:32,001
We'll take her with us to Chennai.

51
00:05:33,376 --> 00:05:36,459
Throwing herself into work
might give her some relief.

52
00:05:42,917 --> 00:05:43,459
Nivi,

53
00:05:44,542 --> 00:05:45,459
it's entirely your decision, dear.

54
00:05:46,292 --> 00:05:48,042
Do you want to stay here,
or go to Chennai?

55
00:06:05,501 --> 00:06:06,126
Nivi...

56
00:06:07,001 --> 00:06:07,626
Nivi...

57
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:17,251
This girl cheated on me.

58
00:06:40,626 --> 00:06:41,626
Just leave her alone for today.

59
00:07:44,751 --> 00:07:45,792
Siri, I want a drink.

60
00:08:02,459 --> 00:08:04,417
Wait, hold on, I'll give everyone one.
Just wait.

61
00:08:04,584 --> 00:08:06,459
What do you want? A quarter?
Okay.

62
00:08:06,584 --> 00:08:08,666
Give him a quarter, man!
Hey, give it to him! Hold on.

63
00:08:08,667 --> 00:08:11,208
Since you said you were taking us to
a new place, I expected something else.

64
00:08:11,209 --> 00:08:12,291
What is this, why is it like this?

65
00:08:12,292 --> 00:08:14,084
This... this is the real Chennai.

66
00:08:15,084 --> 00:08:16,417
Hey, it is falling on us!

67
00:08:16,626 --> 00:08:18,584
Brother, I’ll tell him.
- Hey, watch it! There are ladies here!

68
00:08:19,292 --> 00:08:21,042
Dad, aren't you cold? I'm so cold.

69
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,042
Order, order!

70
00:08:23,042 --> 00:08:25,084
Dad, I already had my bath.
You're the one who woke me up!

71
00:08:25,584 --> 00:08:27,167
Why is he talking to thin air?

72
00:08:28,376 --> 00:08:29,334
Can we get out of here?

73
00:08:31,209 --> 00:08:32,126
It’s fine. It’s okay.

74
00:08:32,501 --> 00:08:33,417
I’ll go get it myself.

75
00:08:34,126 --> 00:08:34,667
Nivi!

76
00:08:35,459 --> 00:08:36,791
Hey, you go with her.

77
00:08:36,792 --> 00:08:38,459
Hey Nivi, stop! I’m coming too!

78
00:08:39,334 --> 00:08:41,666
If you'd just brought the drinks home like
she asked, it would've been fine.

79
00:08:41,667 --> 00:08:43,251
Was it really necessary to bring her here?

80
00:08:43,376 --> 00:08:44,334
I brought her here on purpose.

81
00:08:45,042 --> 00:08:46,917
What’s the point of just
sitting in a room and drinking?

82
00:08:47,167 --> 00:08:47,876
Look around!

83
00:08:49,167 --> 00:08:50,626
Cool, breezy weather...

84
00:08:53,917 --> 00:08:55,084
a refreshing change of scenery...

85
00:08:58,792 --> 00:09:00,084
and all kinds of new faces to see!

86
00:09:05,001 --> 00:09:06,126
Just listen to the stories they tell!

87
00:09:07,376 --> 00:09:08,584
Greetings to Nadigar! (Actor).

88
00:09:09,001 --> 00:09:11,167
Brother, I'm the makeup artist.

89
00:09:11,292 --> 00:09:12,792
Simbu sir is the actor.

90
00:09:14,042 --> 00:09:15,084
What does "Nadigar" mean, bro?

91
00:09:15,334 --> 00:09:16,167
It means "Actor."

92
00:09:16,876 --> 00:09:18,416
Oh... so you've been saying it without
even knowing what it means?

93
00:09:18,417 --> 00:09:19,250
I’m a Telugu guy, brother!

94
00:09:19,251 --> 00:09:20,584
I only know a little bit of Tamil.

95
00:09:21,209 --> 00:09:22,125
Shall I start the pitch, bro?

96
00:09:22,126 --> 00:09:22,917
Yeah, go ahead.

97
00:09:23,042 --> 00:09:23,459
Super!

98
00:09:26,376 --> 00:09:27,292
Narration to...

99
00:09:27,584 --> 00:09:29,291
Simbu sir's makeup man... Velayudham!

100
00:09:29,292 --> 00:09:30,126
Makeup Chief...

101
00:09:30,709 --> 00:09:31,626
What's your name, brother?

102
00:09:31,834 --> 00:09:32,584
Saravanan.

103
00:09:33,126 --> 00:09:34,084
Ah, Sharva bro!

104
00:09:34,834 --> 00:09:36,126
Let's just for our safety!

105
00:09:43,251 --> 00:09:45,584
From the eyes... a massive zoom shot!

106
00:09:46,001 --> 00:09:47,209
First shot of the movie

107
00:09:47,376 --> 00:09:48,459
Hero Introduction!

108
00:09:48,626 --> 00:09:52,751
Up in the air, 25 trains go
Dhada-dhada-dhada-dhada!

109
00:09:53,542 --> 00:09:54,334
what happened?

110
00:09:54,626 --> 00:09:55,709
An accident happened, brother.

111
00:09:57,334 --> 00:09:59,501
And in that accident, the Hero
goes completely blind!

112
00:09:59,792 --> 00:10:00,917
The Heroine goes completely deaf!

113
00:10:01,126 --> 00:10:03,834
They're both get admitted in the same hospital,
lying in beds right next to each other!

114
00:10:04,292 --> 00:10:06,751
The Hero can see the Heroine, but
he can’t hear her speak!

115
00:10:07,042 --> 00:10:09,667
The Heroine can hear the Hero, but
she can’t see him! Pure tragedy!

116
00:10:09,834 --> 00:10:14,667
Then, just like in the movie "Thiru"
we drop a sad Anirudh BGM

117
00:10:16,167 --> 00:10:18,959
And then... A cut here!
A cut there! A cut here!

118
00:10:19,126 --> 00:10:20,958
A cut here! A cut there!

119
00:10:20,959 --> 00:10:24,916
Cut! Cut! Cut! Cut! Cut! Oh man,

120
00:10:24,917 --> 00:10:29,042
The audience in the theatre
will cry their hearts out.

121
00:10:35,834 --> 00:10:37,167
By the interval, suddenly...

122
00:10:37,459 --> 00:10:37,959
STOP!!

123
00:10:39,876 --> 00:10:41,084
What kind of story is this?!

124
00:10:41,417 --> 00:10:44,084
You’ve been roaming around me for a
whole week just to tell me this story?!

125
00:10:44,209 --> 00:10:45,333
I spent the whole week
developing the script, brother!

126
00:10:45,334 --> 00:10:46,709
What exactly did you develop?!

127
00:10:46,917 --> 00:10:47,792
Shut your mouth and get lost!

128
00:10:49,001 --> 00:10:50,501
I have a horror story too!
Should I pitch that?

129
00:10:50,667 --> 00:10:51,167
GET LOST!

130
00:10:56,001 --> 00:10:56,834
Should we call him over?

131
00:10:58,251 --> 00:10:58,917
Hello, brother!

132
00:11:02,001 --> 00:11:02,792
Me?

133
00:11:03,126 --> 00:11:03,667
Yes, brother,

134
00:11:04,376 --> 00:11:06,001
We're Telugu too.
Let's get to know each other.

135
00:11:06,209 --> 00:11:08,291
Once you get to know me,
you'll never want to let me go.

136
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:09,001
The rest is up to you guys.

137
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:09,875
Oh, nothing.

138
00:11:09,876 --> 00:11:11,334
We just saw how those guys
managed to get rid of you. Come here.

139
00:11:11,709 --> 00:11:13,667
Damn it! I lost all my dignity
in the very first introduction!

140
00:11:13,959 --> 00:11:15,000
They just don't get the story.

141
00:11:15,001 --> 00:11:16,167
Even getting a chance to meet
the heroes is a nightmare.

142
00:11:17,251 --> 00:11:18,209
What's your problem?

143
00:11:18,751 --> 00:11:19,833
That's the reality of this industry, brother.

144
00:11:19,834 --> 00:11:20,792
No one gives newcomers a chance.

145
00:11:21,084 --> 00:11:21,958
But the moment you score a single hit,

146
00:11:21,959 --> 00:11:24,001
all these producers will come running
to your house with advance cheques!

147
00:11:27,292 --> 00:11:28,334
Can I tell you something, brother?

148
00:11:28,792 --> 00:11:31,791
If you look from here, even the sun looks tiny.

149
00:11:31,792 --> 00:11:33,751
That doesn't mean the sun is actually small...

150
00:11:34,042 --> 00:11:35,334
it just means the people looking at it are far away.

151
00:11:36,376 --> 00:11:37,167
Who the hell is this guy?

152
00:11:37,292 --> 00:11:38,084
What is he blabbering about?

153
00:11:38,792 --> 00:11:39,792
Our idiots are here, right?

154
00:11:40,209 --> 00:11:41,459
They'll cling to anyone they come across.

155
00:11:42,042 --> 00:11:42,667
Bloody hell!

156
00:11:43,376 --> 00:11:45,334
You look pretty frustrated.
Want to grab a beer?

157
00:11:45,876 --> 00:11:47,501
No, brother. I'll just eat.

158
00:11:48,292 --> 00:11:50,584
Anyway, why are you carrying all
this luggage? Where are you from?

159
00:11:51,084 --> 00:11:51,709
Nellore, brother.

160
00:11:52,876 --> 00:11:53,626
Is your family back there?

161
00:11:54,126 --> 00:11:56,001
I don't have anyone, brother.
Care of the orphanage.

162
00:11:56,584 --> 00:11:57,209
Oh. What's your name?

163
00:11:57,792 --> 00:11:58,334
S.S.

164
00:11:58,834 --> 00:11:59,626
Like S.S. Rajamouli?

165
00:12:00,834 --> 00:12:01,667
Steven Shankar.

166
00:12:02,917 --> 00:12:03,917
Steven Shankar?

167
00:12:04,084 --> 00:12:04,709
What kind of name is that?

168
00:12:05,209 --> 00:12:08,291
I’m a huge fan of Steven Spielberg
and Director Shankar, brother.

169
00:12:08,292 --> 00:12:09,501
So I combined them and gave myself that name.

170
00:12:11,292 --> 00:12:11,792
Bro...

171
00:12:12,417 --> 00:12:13,583
I have a doubt.

172
00:12:13,584 --> 00:12:15,417
With such a massive film industry right
there in Hyderabad,

173
00:12:15,667 --> 00:12:16,501
why did you come all the way down to Chennai?

174
00:12:17,292 --> 00:12:19,583
Brother, my scripts are heart-wrenching
emotional stories

175
00:12:19,584 --> 00:12:20,542
They only work with the Tamil nativity here.

176
00:12:21,084 --> 00:12:22,542
Our Telugu audience just can't
handle that kind of raw emotion!

177
00:12:23,542 --> 00:12:25,792
This guy is a total crackpot.
All show, no substance.

178
00:12:26,459 --> 00:12:27,375
I really don't think so.

179
00:12:27,376 --> 00:12:28,709
Can't you hear the sheer
overacting in his voice?

180
00:12:30,959 --> 00:12:32,417
You guys saw right through me, huh?
Sorry.

181
00:12:33,126 --> 00:12:34,126
Leave it, brother.

182
00:12:34,626 --> 00:12:36,209
Nobody understands the true
value of this Steven.

183
00:12:36,501 --> 00:12:38,208
Like I was saying... if you look from here,
even the sun looks tiny

184
00:12:38,209 --> 00:12:38,876
Hey, stop! Stop!

185
00:12:39,084 --> 00:12:39,417
Stop.

186
00:12:39,876 --> 00:12:40,833
No, brother, it is apt for the situation.

187
00:12:40,834 --> 00:12:41,875
Please let me finish the scene!
Please, brother!

188
00:12:41,876 --> 00:12:43,417
Please, brother!
- Brother, brother...

189
00:12:43,876 --> 00:12:44,792
You've got real fire in you.

190
00:12:45,126 --> 00:12:45,959
I get it now.

191
00:12:46,209 --> 00:12:47,417
You are definitely going to become
a huge director one day.

192
00:12:47,792 --> 00:12:48,458
Thanks, brother.

193
00:12:48,459 --> 00:12:49,626
At least you recognized my talent.

194
00:12:49,834 --> 00:12:50,959
But... once you become a big director,

195
00:12:51,209 --> 00:12:52,084
you have to give me
a role in your movie, alright?

196
00:12:52,751 --> 00:12:54,626
I don't need a big role.

197
00:12:54,876 --> 00:12:56,376
Something like Raghava
Lawrence's role in Don,

198
00:12:56,751 --> 00:12:59,001
or Vivek's in Sivaji, is enough for me.

199
00:12:59,792 --> 00:13:01,459
Is he still obsessed with movies?

200
00:13:02,376 --> 00:13:04,083
Just stay in touch, okay?

201
00:13:04,084 --> 00:13:04,792
You touched my heart, brother!

202
00:13:06,084 --> 00:13:07,042
Here, type your number in!

203
00:13:07,917 --> 00:13:08,334
Give it here.

204
00:13:09,209 --> 00:13:10,959
The world is a very small place, brother!
- Very small.

205
00:13:11,209 --> 00:13:12,416
Such a union is a miracle.

206
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:15,167
I must help you, and you must help me!
That's how it works!

207
00:13:15,459 --> 00:13:16,709
Okay guys, let's leave.

208
00:13:18,459 --> 00:13:19,626
Alright, Steven.
I'll catch you later then.

209
00:13:20,417 --> 00:13:21,666
Nivi, We'll be waiting near the parking lot.

210
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:22,917
Finish up and come.

211
00:13:23,501 --> 00:13:23,959
Brother...

212
00:13:25,334 --> 00:13:26,126
You told me to stay in touch!

213
00:13:26,626 --> 00:13:27,376
You already gave me your number, didn't you?

214
00:13:27,834 --> 00:13:28,667
Won't you ask me for my address?

215
00:13:28,917 --> 00:13:29,376
Fine. Tell me.

216
00:13:36,417 --> 00:13:36,959
Just a minute...

217
00:13:37,917 --> 00:13:38,959
Hey, Surya.. no.

218
00:13:39,834 --> 00:13:40,417
Say No.

219
00:13:43,501 --> 00:13:44,251
It’s not possible, brother.

220
00:13:44,917 --> 00:13:46,876
If Puri had asked Ravi Teja like
this would he ever say No?

221
00:13:49,251 --> 00:13:50,042
He'd never say no...

222
00:13:50,417 --> 00:13:51,167
Hang on a second.

223
00:13:52,584 --> 00:13:54,000
Hey, come on guys!

224
00:13:54,001 --> 00:13:55,501
What now?
- What now?

225
00:13:55,667 --> 00:13:57,626
Please listen to me guys...
I'll become the next Ravi Teja.

226
00:14:02,542 --> 00:14:03,001
Madam!

227
00:14:03,751 --> 00:14:04,251
Hello!

228
00:14:05,834 --> 00:14:08,667
Are you with them, or did you just
sit here because the seats were empty?

229
00:14:10,167 --> 00:14:11,334
Siri, shall we go?

230
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:12,667
Wait, just a minute!

231
00:14:13,626 --> 00:14:15,292
Oh, so you are in the same group.

232
00:14:15,709 --> 00:14:16,584
I'm Steven Shankar.

233
00:14:16,792 --> 00:14:19,126
Trust me, once you get to know me,
you'll never want to let me go.

234
00:14:19,251 --> 00:14:19,791
Let him come, man.

235
00:14:19,792 --> 00:14:20,625
Siri, come...
- We will add him in split-wise.

236
00:14:20,626 --> 00:14:21,167
- Ah, I'm coming.

237
00:14:22,167 --> 00:14:25,416
If anything goes wrong because of him tomorrow
I'll deal with you then.

238
00:14:25,417 --> 00:14:26,542
Then it'll be on you.
– Don't worry. I'll handle it.

239
00:14:27,417 --> 00:14:28,584
Steven!

240
00:14:31,376 --> 00:14:32,084
Thanks, bro.

241
00:14:49,501 --> 00:14:51,334
Bye, brother.
- Okay, bye.

242
00:14:51,751 --> 00:14:52,501
Good morning, Madam!

243
00:14:54,376 --> 00:14:55,084
Good morning, Madam

244
00:14:56,167 --> 00:14:58,001
Surya brought him here despite my objections.

245
00:14:58,167 --> 00:15:00,376
If he's bothering you, just say the word,
and I'll send him out.

246
00:15:03,376 --> 00:15:08,334
"Chennai… Chennai… Chennai…
show us a brand-new path."

247
00:15:09,751 --> 00:15:14,376
"There are so many mysteries…
come, unravel the tangles for us."

248
00:15:16,376 --> 00:15:18,126
"One is this way"

249
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,042
"the other is that way.. different as can be"

250
00:15:22,959 --> 00:15:25,792
"Yet both have found their way to you."

251
00:15:26,167 --> 00:15:28,959
"Look upon them with grace, oh precious city,"

252
00:15:29,334 --> 00:15:32,417
"Not everyone can carry every burden."

253
00:15:32,584 --> 00:15:34,584
"Don't let the tension grow;"

254
00:15:35,459 --> 00:15:37,166
"Give us moments of joy,
give us wise counsel, "

255
00:15:37,167 --> 00:15:38,834
"give us enough time to live."

256
00:15:42,126 --> 00:15:45,251
"Grant us the daring to read the
rhythm of the rising and falling waves."

257
00:15:48,626 --> 00:15:51,751
"A girl and a boy…
what’s going to happen here?"

258
00:15:55,084 --> 00:15:58,209
"When they become one,
A beautiful miracle begins."

259
00:16:00,792 --> 00:16:01,625
Brother!

260
00:16:01,626 --> 00:16:02,750
No, no. You can't go inside.

261
00:16:02,751 --> 00:16:04,084
Please let me go.
- Go back. You're not allowed to enter.

262
00:16:04,751 --> 00:16:05,167
Brother!

263
00:16:05,417 --> 00:16:06,209
What's the matter? Tell me.

264
00:16:06,667 --> 00:16:07,667
I'm here as a junior artist.

265
00:16:08,084 --> 00:16:10,084
When will the hero be here?
I need to narrate a story to him.

266
00:16:12,751 --> 00:16:14,375
Hey! Why are you drinking from that cup?

267
00:16:14,376 --> 00:16:16,042
Put it back and use a paper cup instead.

268
00:16:18,001 --> 00:16:22,876
"Chennai… Chennai… Chennai…
let us shed the burdens of yesterday."

269
00:16:24,667 --> 00:16:29,209
"Like a brilliant full-moon sky,
bathe our lives in soft moonlight."

270
00:16:30,876 --> 00:16:32,583
Why is she starting so early in the morning, man?

271
00:16:32,584 --> 00:16:35,834
Look, she's already in a bad mood.
Don't make it worse, or you'll pay for it later.

272
00:16:37,251 --> 00:16:43,376
"You are the clever city that raised
a bus conductor into a global Superstar."

273
00:16:43,959 --> 00:16:48,959
"You've crowned film stars as Chief Ministers,"

274
00:16:50,251 --> 00:16:53,501
"You mold a thousand dreams
into reality in mere minutes;"

275
00:16:56,709 --> 00:16:59,751
"Now, tie the knot that joins
these two hearts in a single second."

276
00:17:03,459 --> 00:17:04,625
Hey, hey! You can't go in.

277
00:17:04,626 --> 00:17:05,791
Brother, just one minute.
I'll go upstairs and be right back.

278
00:17:05,792 --> 00:17:06,875
Didn't you see the sign?
No, no, you can't enter.

279
00:17:06,876 --> 00:17:08,251
Brother, just one minute.
- I told you to go outside!

280
00:17:09,709 --> 00:17:12,876
"When they become one,
A beautiful miracle begins."

281
00:19:01,084 --> 00:19:02,792
Why is the room clean?

282
00:19:12,251 --> 00:19:13,334
Who came into my room?

283
00:19:13,542 --> 00:19:14,126
What happened?

284
00:19:14,542 --> 00:19:17,126
I told you I need some time to get over this, didn't I?

285
00:19:17,376 --> 00:19:19,334
Until then, I don't need any of your
stupid brainwash...

286
00:19:19,709 --> 00:19:20,626
What happened?

287
00:19:20,959 --> 00:19:24,209
Siri, if I'm being a disturbance here,
just tell me. I'll go stay in a PG

288
00:19:24,459 --> 00:19:28,126
But don't do this... don't embarrass
me by writing cheap captions like this!

289
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:29,584
Captions?

290
00:19:34,334 --> 00:19:38,167
“An oar may break, but the boat shouldn't stop…
A love may fail, but life must go on.”

291
00:19:38,834 --> 00:19:40,209
This was definitely done by Steven.

292
00:19:40,626 --> 00:19:42,750
If she finds out, she’ll cause a scene again.

293
00:19:42,751 --> 00:19:43,792
Fine. Let's go and handle it somehow.

294
00:19:44,292 --> 00:19:46,709
Ahh! who wrote this anyway?
– I did. I did. I did

295
00:19:47,209 --> 00:19:49,792
I just wanted to create a positive
atmosphere for you.

296
00:19:50,376 --> 00:19:51,042
You..?

297
00:19:51,376 --> 00:19:52,084
Why? Am I not allowed to write?

298
00:19:52,626 --> 00:19:53,334
Hello, brother...

299
00:19:54,876 --> 00:19:58,834
I thought credit-stealing only happened in the
film industry, but you're doing it out here too?

300
00:19:59,876 --> 00:20:00,709
Isn't that wrong, brother?

301
00:20:00,917 --> 00:20:01,792
Just shut up and go inside.

302
00:20:02,084 --> 00:20:05,042
Madam, the whole "credit and debit"
belongs to me!

303
00:20:07,292 --> 00:20:08,334
I wrote the entire thing.

304
00:20:08,751 --> 00:20:09,459
It’s good, isn’t it, madam?

305
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:10,834
Who the hell are you?

306
00:20:12,167 --> 00:20:14,792
I've been noticing you since you got here.
Why are you always trying to annoy me?

307
00:20:15,084 --> 00:20:16,751
And how dare you come into my room?

308
00:20:17,209 --> 00:20:19,542
What right do you have to involve
yourself in my personal life?!

309
00:20:20,167 --> 00:20:21,833
I just thought it might
make you feel a little better...

310
00:20:21,834 --> 00:20:23,042
Who the hell are you to make me feel better?

311
00:20:23,917 --> 00:20:26,626
Just because we gave you a place
to stay doesn't mean you're one of us!

312
00:20:27,376 --> 00:20:28,209
Be in your limits.

313
00:20:28,376 --> 00:20:29,666
Maybe he didn't mean to.
Let it go.

314
00:20:29,667 --> 00:20:30,917
Actually, I should be blaming all of you first!

315
00:20:32,584 --> 00:20:35,292
For picking up some random orphan off the
streets and bringing him into our home!

316
00:20:35,917 --> 00:20:37,417
Shouldn't he have some basic manners?

317
00:20:40,834 --> 00:20:41,792
Okay... just go get ready for work. Go.

318
00:20:42,209 --> 00:20:42,626
Disgusting.

319
00:21:31,334 --> 00:21:32,167
Hey, Steven

320
00:21:32,417 --> 00:21:33,417
don't take it to heart.

321
00:21:33,626 --> 00:21:36,334
She's carrying a lot of frustration.
That's why she snapped like that.

322
00:21:36,792 --> 00:21:39,584
I'm heading to the office.
Take care, okay?

323
00:21:48,626 --> 00:21:49,959
Brother, one full bottle.

324
00:22:36,917 --> 00:22:37,542
Steven...

325
00:22:38,584 --> 00:22:39,417
get on, let’s go home.

326
00:22:49,167 --> 00:22:51,000
Not like that man, you’re supposed
to eat that with a fork.

327
00:22:51,001 --> 00:22:52,042
Eat properly, man.

328
00:22:52,709 --> 00:22:54,834
He’s a total savage;
he won’t get it. Just leave him be.

329
00:23:02,126 --> 00:23:04,376
What’s up with Nivi?
Is she okay?

330
00:23:05,376 --> 00:23:07,792
Why don't you go ask her?
- No, no. I’m fine, man.

331
00:23:09,667 --> 00:23:10,542
I don’t want.

332
00:23:10,709 --> 00:23:11,792
Have some starters at least.

333
00:23:12,667 --> 00:23:14,876
Look, he looks like someone famous.

334
00:23:17,501 --> 00:23:19,042
Hey, it's P. Vasu sir!

335
00:23:19,292 --> 00:23:20,376
Wait, who is he?

336
00:23:21,167 --> 00:23:22,167
He’s a massive director!

337
00:23:22,292 --> 00:23:24,834
He’s the one who made Chandramukhi.
"Laka-laka-laka"! That’s him.

338
00:23:25,001 --> 00:23:26,416
Sir, I’m getting too many calls.

339
00:23:26,417 --> 00:23:26,750
Okay sir.

340
00:23:26,751 --> 00:23:27,791
Fine, you keep the phone with you.

341
00:23:27,792 --> 00:23:30,626
He recently started a production house;
he’s producing films now.

342
00:23:30,917 --> 00:23:31,917
How do you know all that?

343
00:23:32,459 --> 00:23:35,209
Well, I went for a couple of auditions
recently and... I failed.

344
00:23:37,792 --> 00:23:38,417
Don't you laugh!

345
00:23:38,584 --> 00:23:39,541
Why shouldn't I laugh?

346
00:23:39,542 --> 00:23:40,917
I gave it my best shot, okay?
It just didn't work out.

347
00:23:42,126 --> 00:23:45,709
Hey Nivi, don't go asking for any favors
or roles for me. He won’t give me anyway.

348
00:23:46,334 --> 00:23:48,084
While the movie is still being shot,
- Yes, sir.

349
00:23:48,209 --> 00:23:50,708
we need to close the OTT deal.
- Definitely, sir.

350
00:23:50,709 --> 00:23:52,001
Then, with that director...
- Excuse me, sir.

351
00:23:53,167 --> 00:23:54,209
Very nice to meet you.

352
00:23:54,626 --> 00:23:55,792
I’m a huge fan of your movies.

353
00:23:56,001 --> 00:23:56,501
Thank you.

354
00:23:58,001 --> 00:23:59,500
Sir...

355
00:23:59,501 --> 00:24:00,751
What I am saying is...
- Sir...

356
00:24:02,126 --> 00:24:04,501
I have a friend, an aspiring filmmaker...

357
00:24:04,709 --> 00:24:07,792
actually, not a friend, just someone I know.

358
00:24:08,126 --> 00:24:10,001
But he’s very passionate.

359
00:24:11,126 --> 00:24:14,709
If you could give him a chance,
it would be a huge help to him.

360
00:24:15,209 --> 00:24:18,834
Madam, Sir is in the middle of an important meeting.
Please don't interrupt.

361
00:24:19,126 --> 00:24:19,834
I'm sorry, sir.

362
00:24:20,001 --> 00:24:22,292
I’ll wait until your meeting is finished.

363
00:24:23,084 --> 00:24:26,001
You handle that OTT deal yourself.
- I'm on it, sir.

364
00:24:48,876 --> 00:24:50,876
You know, a police officer
shouldn't do something like this, right?

365
00:24:51,084 --> 00:24:53,084
why would rules matter to a killer like you?

366
00:24:53,792 --> 00:24:56,001
Since we are talking to him gently without
beating him, he is blabbering needlessly.

367
00:24:56,376 --> 00:24:58,916
Stop wasting our time unnecessarily
and respectfully tell us the whole truth.

368
00:24:58,917 --> 00:25:01,501
I’ve submitted all the files today.
Tell them to cross-check everything.

369
00:25:03,959 --> 00:25:04,917
– Okay, bye.

370
00:25:38,126 --> 00:25:40,167
If you want to say sorry,
you can just say it directly.

371
00:25:41,792 --> 00:25:43,792
Hey, take this and look at it first.

372
00:25:51,959 --> 00:25:54,459
I like Tamil movies,
but I can’t actually read the language.

373
00:25:55,042 --> 00:25:56,834
Seriously? Look at it properly!

374
00:25:59,167 --> 00:26:00,417
I don't need your number, thanks.

375
00:26:03,209 --> 00:26:04,501
That’s a producer’s number.

376
00:26:04,959 --> 00:26:06,251
I’ve already spoken to him for you.

377
00:26:07,126 --> 00:26:09,542
You have a meeting tomorrow at 10:00 AM.
Go meet him.

378
00:26:11,417 --> 00:26:14,584
Stop complaining about directors being useless.

379
00:26:15,126 --> 00:26:18,292
If you’ve got real talent,
go pitch your story and prove it.

380
00:26:19,042 --> 00:26:22,084
Show your talent there, not on bedroom walls.

381
00:27:05,209 --> 00:27:06,876
Excuse me, who are you?

382
00:27:07,459 --> 00:27:10,459
Steven Shankar.
I’m here to meet Vasu sir.

383
00:27:10,792 --> 00:27:12,084
Give it ten minutes.
Please, have a seat.

384
00:27:29,584 --> 00:27:30,084
Tea, sir?

385
00:27:30,751 --> 00:27:32,251
Oh, is it for sir?
- Give it to me. I'll take it to him.

386
00:27:32,626 --> 00:27:33,626
No, sir. The tea is for you.

387
00:27:36,084 --> 00:27:37,083
For me?

388
00:27:37,084 --> 00:27:38,084
Yes, for you.

389
00:27:46,459 --> 00:27:46,876
Brother...

390
00:27:47,167 --> 00:27:47,626
Sir!

391
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:49,084
Thanks.

392
00:27:49,292 --> 00:27:50,042
It's okay sir.

393
00:28:07,834 --> 00:28:08,958
Give this to the director.

394
00:28:08,959 --> 00:28:09,333
Okay Madam.

395
00:28:09,334 --> 00:28:11,126
Excuse me.
Sir is asking to see you now.

396
00:28:13,459 --> 00:28:14,167
Good morning, sir.

397
00:28:14,917 --> 00:28:16,917
Ah, come in, David.

398
00:28:24,334 --> 00:28:25,667
My name is Steven Shankar, sir.

399
00:28:28,209 --> 00:28:28,792
Sit down.

400
00:28:31,001 --> 00:28:32,667
You’re from the Telugu industry, right?
- Yes, sir.

401
00:28:33,417 --> 00:28:36,959
So, why are you trying your
luck here instead of Hyderabad?

402
00:28:37,167 --> 00:28:41,126
Well, my stories are so heart-wrenching, sir...
I don't think Telugu audiences could handle them!

403
00:28:42,917 --> 00:28:44,917
Honestly, looking at you, I don't feel like lying.

404
00:28:45,626 --> 00:28:49,292
The truth is, nobody’s giving me a break back home.
That’s why I’m here trying my best.

405
00:29:24,042 --> 00:29:25,625
Hey, check if the light is on!

406
00:29:25,626 --> 00:29:26,250
Okay Brother.

407
00:29:26,251 --> 00:29:27,251
Bro... It's on.

408
00:29:31,792 --> 00:29:33,251
Hey, Steven is here!

409
00:29:34,292 --> 00:29:35,250
Come on, come over here!

410
00:29:35,251 --> 00:29:36,959
Wait, why does he look so happy?

411
00:29:37,209 --> 00:29:39,209
Hey boss, did the producer like the story?

412
00:29:39,334 --> 00:29:40,459
Can't you tell by his face?

413
00:29:40,667 --> 00:29:42,751
Is my role confirmed?
Can I quit my job now?

414
00:29:42,917 --> 00:29:45,167
So my photo with Surya is a sure thing, right?

415
00:29:45,459 --> 00:29:47,501
What happened, Steven?
What did the producer say?

416
00:29:47,709 --> 00:29:49,792
The producer said the story was
terrible and asked me to leave.

417
00:29:51,667 --> 00:29:52,709
You Idiot?

418
00:29:52,876 --> 00:29:53,709
What?

419
00:29:53,959 --> 00:29:55,667
Then why are you acting like you just hit the jackpot?

420
00:29:55,876 --> 00:29:58,251
I think you've overestimated me, bro.

421
00:29:58,459 --> 00:30:02,001
I'm the kind of guy security throws out
before I even get into a production office.

422
00:30:02,126 --> 00:30:04,376
But today, I actually got to pitch
my story to a big-time producer!

423
00:30:04,542 --> 00:30:05,209
That's more than enough for me.

424
00:30:05,792 --> 00:30:08,001
I'll be on cloud nine for the next ten days.

425
00:30:08,251 --> 00:30:09,417
What more could I ask for, bro?

426
00:30:10,417 --> 00:30:11,792
Did you hear what your director said?

427
00:30:12,126 --> 00:30:13,417
He should be ashamed of himself
for talking like that.

428
00:30:14,084 --> 00:30:14,876
Ashamed?

429
00:30:15,459 --> 00:30:18,292
Bro, you don't know what I'm really capable of.

430
00:30:18,584 --> 00:30:19,792
I'm not that big a deal.

431
00:30:20,376 --> 00:30:21,959
Do you know how I ended up in Chennai?

432
00:30:22,542 --> 00:30:26,751
My pastor knew someone who
worked in a film office here,

433
00:30:27,042 --> 00:30:29,667
Trusting him without a second
thought, I came to Chennai.

434
00:30:31,792 --> 00:30:34,209
Just two days...
only two days.

435
00:30:34,792 --> 00:30:38,042
On the third day, when I went to his room,
I found my bag dumped outside.

436
00:30:39,542 --> 00:30:41,667
When I called him, he'd blocked my number.

437
00:30:42,792 --> 00:30:45,209
I had nowhere to stay and no one I could turn to.

438
00:30:46,542 --> 00:30:50,084
You know those train compartments
at the railway station, bro?

439
00:30:50,959 --> 00:30:52,001
That's where I used to sleep.

440
00:30:55,376 --> 00:30:57,376
The little money I brought
ran out within a week.

441
00:30:58,376 --> 00:30:59,584
I didn't even have money to eat.

442
00:30:59,876 --> 00:31:02,501
I thought about taking up some job to survive,

443
00:31:03,001 --> 00:31:04,834
but I was afraid I'd get used to earning money...

444
00:31:05,001 --> 00:31:06,751
and end up neglecting
my dream of making films.

445
00:31:08,126 --> 00:31:09,376
So, I didn't take up any other job.

446
00:31:14,792 --> 00:31:19,959
Since I hadn't eaten anything for two days,
my stomach was in excruciating pain.

447
00:31:22,917 --> 00:31:27,917
But still, no matter what happened,
I wanted to be in films and make movies.

448
00:31:28,334 --> 00:31:30,292
I never thought about anything else, brother.

449
00:31:32,126 --> 00:31:33,209
But one day...

450
00:31:35,042 --> 00:31:39,834
right here on my back, in a spot I couldn't reach,
a painful boil appeared.

451
00:31:42,709 --> 00:31:44,626
It grew bigger day by day.

452
00:31:44,959 --> 00:31:47,876
I wanted to get it treated,
but I didn't even have money for a hospital.

453
00:31:48,876 --> 00:31:50,876
You know those red brick shards?

454
00:31:51,626 --> 00:31:55,376
I ground two of them together into a powder
and applied that to the wound, brother.

455
00:32:00,876 --> 00:32:02,376
The pain was excruciating.

456
00:32:03,251 --> 00:32:07,834
That was when I felt I couldn't survive
here anymore and should just leave.

457
00:32:11,001 --> 00:32:13,001
That’s when I met all of you.

458
00:32:13,709 --> 00:32:18,126
You don't realize what a significant
place you hold in my life.

459
00:32:22,917 --> 00:32:24,417
Madam, especially you.

460
00:32:24,917 --> 00:32:27,334
When you scolded me the other day,
I felt deeply hurt.

461
00:32:27,667 --> 00:32:31,251
But later I realized,
you scolding me is nothing.

462
00:32:33,584 --> 00:32:36,501
I’m just an orphan with no name or home;

463
00:32:36,959 --> 00:32:38,459
I’ve been insulted by many people before…

464
00:32:40,751 --> 00:32:41,334
But...

465
00:32:42,459 --> 00:32:46,376
But after scolding me, you actually
felt bad for me and helped me out.

466
00:32:48,501 --> 00:32:49,376
That put you on a high pedestal in my heart.

467
00:32:51,126 --> 00:32:52,959
That is where you stand in my eyes, Madam.

468
00:32:54,876 --> 00:32:55,792
Fix that in your mind…

469
00:32:57,042 --> 00:33:00,459
From now on, this is your
stature in Steven's eyes.

470
00:33:02,292 --> 00:33:05,626
Madam, if you ever need anything,
just snap your fingers.

471
00:33:05,959 --> 00:33:09,751
actually, don't even snap, just think of it,
and I’ll be at your feet.

472
00:33:11,751 --> 00:33:13,333
From now on, forget just scolding me;

473
00:33:13,334 --> 00:33:17,459
even if you look at me like a stray dog,
I will never leave your side.

474
00:33:19,667 --> 00:33:23,084
Even if I am on my deathbed,
if you call out to me with love just once,

475
00:33:23,292 --> 00:33:25,501
I’ll come flying to you like a Pegasus.

476
00:33:27,876 --> 00:33:30,334
From this day on, you are my goddess,

477
00:33:32,042 --> 00:33:33,209
and I am your humble servant.

478
00:33:46,876 --> 00:33:47,376
That's it.

479
00:34:22,792 --> 00:34:24,792
"Sparkling star.."

480
00:34:25,417 --> 00:34:27,751
"oh sparkling star.."

481
00:34:28,376 --> 00:34:32,751
"Have you descended here with all your heart?"

482
00:34:34,542 --> 00:34:39,501
Leaving the skies behind for this mischievous soul,"

483
00:34:40,209 --> 00:34:44,792
"You came to earth as the goddess of my silence."

484
00:34:45,417 --> 00:34:50,376
"From this moment on,
I wish to live as your devoted one,"

485
00:34:50,876 --> 00:34:55,876
"Serving you with all my heart, every single day."

486
00:34:56,001 --> 00:34:58,001
"Sparkling star.."

487
00:34:58,626 --> 00:35:00,959
"oh sparkling star.."

488
00:35:01,542 --> 00:35:05,917
"Have you descended here with all your heart?"

489
00:35:35,292 --> 00:35:40,459
"I was like a creature trapped
inside a lonely well,"

490
00:35:40,792 --> 00:35:45,959
"Until you immersed me in a garden of flowers."

491
00:35:46,376 --> 00:35:51,376
"I was a boat drifting without a shore,"

492
00:35:51,917 --> 00:35:57,000
"You found me like a lighthouse on my way."

493
00:35:57,001 --> 00:36:02,167
"Yesterday was darkness, even in broad daylight,"

494
00:36:02,501 --> 00:36:07,542
"Today, even midnight feels like dawn."

495
00:36:08,251 --> 00:36:13,250
"You became a rainbow on the
canvas of my empty life."

496
00:36:13,251 --> 00:36:15,251
"Sparkling star.."

497
00:36:15,751 --> 00:36:18,084
"oh sparkling star.."

498
00:36:18,667 --> 00:36:23,042
"Have you descended here with all your heart?"

499
00:36:57,334 --> 00:36:58,459
Steven, what’s wrong?

500
00:36:58,792 --> 00:37:00,042
You guys carry on.
Please, go ahead.

501
00:37:00,459 --> 00:37:01,876
Hey, what exactly is your problem?

502
00:37:02,251 --> 00:37:03,834
And who are you to apply the bandage on her?

503
00:37:04,042 --> 00:37:06,291
Excuse me?
You just showed up the other day.

504
00:37:06,292 --> 00:37:07,584
I’ve been her friend forever.

505
00:37:07,792 --> 00:37:10,167
Oh, really? Well, did you ever tell her
that you’re her slave?

506
00:37:10,501 --> 00:37:11,001
What?!

507
00:37:11,251 --> 00:37:13,251
Since you never said that, you have absolutely
no right to put that bandage on her.

508
00:37:14,834 --> 00:37:16,417
Man, I give up.
Fine, you do it yourself.

509
00:37:16,542 --> 00:37:17,292
Then get out of here!

510
00:37:18,667 --> 00:37:19,916
I need to go kick Surya first.

511
00:37:19,917 --> 00:37:20,667
Idiot.

512
00:37:39,292 --> 00:37:44,542
"I'll echo through the night like a king's melody,"

513
00:37:44,667 --> 00:37:49,917
"Rest peacefully in my sweetest lullaby."

514
00:37:50,167 --> 00:37:55,500
"I'll become a Bharathiraja masterpiece,"

515
00:37:55,501 --> 00:38:00,834
"Lose yourself in a world painted with colors."

516
00:38:01,001 --> 00:38:11,417
"I'll be your Vel whenever you need me,
Smile freely and cherish this moment."

517
00:38:11,959 --> 00:38:17,291
"I'll show you a life that's even
more beautiful than the movies."

518
00:38:17,292 --> 00:38:23,041
"Oh moon-maiden, my radiant light,"

519
00:38:23,042 --> 00:38:27,709
"You are the beautiful glow of my life."

520
00:38:28,751 --> 00:38:33,542
"Whatever your heart desires, just ask for it."

521
00:38:34,376 --> 00:38:39,167
"Take as much happiness as you wish."

522
00:38:39,626 --> 00:38:44,751
"They say every story eventually
comes to an end..."

523
00:38:45,126 --> 00:38:50,876
"But before Goddess Kamakshi,
our story has only just begun"

524
00:38:55,084 --> 00:38:57,459
It doesn’t look like she’s here yet.
- Give her a call.

525
00:39:00,667 --> 00:39:03,876
Oh, there you are!
Auntie, how was the journey?

526
00:39:05,167 --> 00:39:06,584
Are these two ours? Any more?

527
00:39:06,876 --> 00:39:07,417
Come on, this way.

528
00:39:08,001 --> 00:39:10,001
Wait, how much should I pay the porter?

529
00:39:10,667 --> 00:39:12,001
Why is he just walking off with the bags?

530
00:39:12,376 --> 00:39:14,083
Mom, he’s my friend.

531
00:39:14,084 --> 00:39:15,125
A friend?

532
00:39:15,126 --> 00:39:18,834
Looking at that lungi and his whole
get-up, I thought he was a porter! Let's go.

533
00:39:23,001 --> 00:39:25,501
I’m packing some food for you; don’t forget to eat.

534
00:39:26,834 --> 00:39:28,834
Are you even eating on time?

535
00:39:29,042 --> 00:39:30,291
She doesn’t eat a thing, Auntie.

536
00:39:30,292 --> 00:39:33,626
If I offer to make her something,
she only ever asks for an omelet late at night.

537
00:39:38,251 --> 00:39:40,501
Everyone over there is worried about you.

538
00:39:41,042 --> 00:39:43,459
They keep asking when you’re going to get married.

539
00:39:46,501 --> 00:39:48,334
My health hasn't been great lately, Nivi.

540
00:39:49,084 --> 00:39:50,751
If you could just get married...

541
00:39:51,334 --> 00:39:53,334
Mom, did you really come all the way
to Chennai just to talk to me about this?

542
00:39:53,876 --> 00:39:54,917
It’s not that, Nivi...

543
00:39:55,042 --> 00:39:58,126
All you ever care about is what other people think.

544
00:39:59,001 --> 00:40:01,251
Do you even care about my situation?

545
00:40:02,459 --> 00:40:03,251
No...

546
00:40:03,626 --> 00:40:04,917
Steven!
- Yes, Madam?

547
00:40:07,376 --> 00:40:08,542
I’m late for work.

548
00:40:08,834 --> 00:40:12,209
If they’re here to actually stay with me,
tell them they can stay as long as they want.

549
00:40:12,667 --> 00:40:16,876
But if they only came here to talk about this,
book them on the next train back.

550
00:40:33,626 --> 00:40:34,709
He was a good guy.

551
00:40:35,667 --> 00:40:41,126
They were in love for three years,
and before that, they were friends for two years.

552
00:40:42,709 --> 00:40:45,042
He couldn’t bear to spend a single minute away from Nivi.

553
00:40:45,459 --> 00:40:48,751
No matter what happened at our house,
Ajay was always the first one there to help.

554
00:40:49,084 --> 00:40:54,001
He even took your Auntie to Bangalore
personally for her treatment.

555
00:40:55,167 --> 00:40:56,501
Everything was going so well...

556
00:40:57,709 --> 00:40:58,959
I have no idea what went wrong.

557
00:41:00,001 --> 00:41:02,001
He just left on the very day of the wedding.

558
00:41:06,167 --> 00:41:08,167
Your generation is something else.

559
00:41:08,834 --> 00:41:11,459
You stay within a centimeter of sentiments,

560
00:41:12,417 --> 00:41:15,376
but the moment commitment comes up, you run a kilometer away.

561
00:41:16,876 --> 00:41:17,709
Wait, what did you just say, Uncle?

562
00:41:18,251 --> 00:41:24,917
I said, you stay within a centimeter of sentiments,
but run a kilometer away from commitment.

563
00:41:25,834 --> 00:41:27,084
I have to ask, Uncle...

564
00:41:27,209 --> 00:41:29,834
Does the way you're talking even
match the emotion you're in?

565
00:41:29,959 --> 00:41:32,791
Oh, well... it just came out in the flow, you know?

566
00:41:32,792 --> 00:41:33,834
What "flow," Uncle?

567
00:41:34,376 --> 00:41:35,666
Honestly, I can’t even blame you.

568
00:41:35,667 --> 00:41:38,792
It’s all "Guru-ji’s" fault for getting the general
audience addicted to these rhymes and punchlines.

569
00:41:40,084 --> 00:41:42,876
If everyone starts talking in punchlines,
what's left for me to do?

570
00:41:44,834 --> 00:41:45,709
So, are you coming or not?

571
00:41:56,626 --> 00:41:58,042
Dad didn't drink much, did he?

572
00:41:58,209 --> 00:41:59,626
Not nearly as much as you.

573
00:42:02,376 --> 00:42:03,833
Instead of drinking separately like this,

574
00:42:03,834 --> 00:42:08,209
why don't you drink together?
It'd be like sending a message to society.

575
00:42:08,376 --> 00:42:09,876
Steven, please.

576
00:42:10,292 --> 00:42:12,167
What else?
You're always drinking.

577
00:42:12,542 --> 00:42:16,209
Look, the balcony is filled with
beer bottles and cigarette packs.

578
00:42:17,334 --> 00:42:19,751
We should grow some plants.
It brings positivity.

579
00:42:20,042 --> 00:42:21,751
Anyway, how are your trials going?

580
00:42:22,459 --> 00:42:26,125
Trials? My foot! The producer won't
even answer my calls after hearing the story.

581
00:42:26,126 --> 00:42:28,042
I'm just living off your food
and looking for another producer.

582
00:42:29,751 --> 00:42:34,751
When you know this field isn't working out,
why don't you look for something else?

583
00:42:34,917 --> 00:42:39,376
Look, I might die, but I will only die
after making a movie.

584
00:42:40,376 --> 00:42:42,126
Why are you so obsessed with movies?

585
00:42:46,167 --> 00:42:48,501
I must have been around eight years old.

586
00:42:49,084 --> 00:42:51,334
I grew up in an orphanage, as you know.

587
00:42:51,834 --> 00:42:54,501
Donors used to visit our orphanage every Sunday.

588
00:42:54,876 --> 00:42:56,709
They would bring good food and toys.

589
00:42:57,001 --> 00:42:58,667
We used to play all day.

590
00:43:02,876 --> 00:43:06,084
But at night, the same loneliness returned.

591
00:43:06,376 --> 00:43:07,792
I couldn't sleep properly.

592
00:43:09,042 --> 00:43:10,876
That's when our Srinu came along.

593
00:43:13,459 --> 00:43:14,667
Where did you go?

594
00:43:14,917 --> 00:43:17,167
I went to a movie with the money the donors gave.

595
00:43:17,376 --> 00:43:19,209
- To the theater?
- Yes.

596
00:43:19,542 --> 00:43:21,417
It must be just like watching on TV.

597
00:43:21,584 --> 00:43:25,291
What are you saying?
Are theater and TV the same?

598
00:43:25,292 --> 00:43:27,750
On TV, Chiranjeevi is only this small.

599
00:43:27,751 --> 00:43:30,917
But in a theater, he looks as grand as Lord Hanuman.

600
00:43:41,126 --> 00:43:42,292
What he said was true.

601
00:43:42,792 --> 00:43:45,042
It felt like a whole new world.

602
00:43:45,709 --> 00:43:49,126
While watching, I forgot about everything else.

603
00:43:51,042 --> 00:43:54,126
It's like they say, your heart gets full.
That was the feeling.

604
00:43:59,292 --> 00:44:02,751
That's when I realized, why should Steven be lonely?

605
00:44:03,209 --> 00:44:07,042
Chiranjeevi's parents are my parents,
and his friends are my friends.

606
00:44:08,376 --> 00:44:10,126
I myself felt like Chiranjeevi.

607
00:44:14,084 --> 00:44:16,126
Since then, I had no other thoughts.

608
00:44:16,876 --> 00:44:20,501
With age, my passion for movies only grew.

609
00:44:27,792 --> 00:44:29,626
After some time, I started writing stories.

610
00:44:30,084 --> 00:44:33,209
No matter who I met, I would tell them a story.

611
00:44:35,292 --> 00:44:36,541
When they heard it and said,

612
00:44:36,542 --> 00:44:42,417
"Steven, you'll be a director,"
I would get goosebumps all over. Look, even now.

613
00:44:44,251 --> 00:44:45,542
That's when I decided.

614
00:44:45,751 --> 00:44:52,459
One day, "Written and Directed by Steven Shankar"
must appear on the 70mm screen.

615
00:44:53,042 --> 00:44:54,167
That's all fine.

616
00:44:55,417 --> 00:44:57,709
But why are you writing such stories?

617
00:44:59,084 --> 00:45:00,083
What?

618
00:45:00,084 --> 00:45:03,042
I mean, I read one of your stories recently.

619
00:45:03,417 --> 00:45:05,751
How can you read it without my permission?

620
00:45:05,876 --> 00:45:10,042
Oh, please! I couldn't even read past 20 pages.

621
00:45:10,834 --> 00:45:12,042
It was terrible.

622
00:45:12,834 --> 00:45:14,834
That's why I say you should read the whole thing.

623
00:45:15,417 --> 00:45:17,167
You shouldn't give reviews based on just half of it.

624
00:45:18,292 --> 00:45:23,083
There is a scene in a temple
where the hero and heroine...

625
00:45:23,084 --> 00:45:26,042
Yes, scene 14B, night effect, emotional scene.
That one, right?

626
00:45:27,167 --> 00:45:31,084
Was that an emotional scene?
Sorry, I thought it was comedy.

627
00:45:31,292 --> 00:45:34,334
Even then, it didn't make me laugh.
It was very cringe.

628
00:45:35,959 --> 00:45:37,250
Don't ever ask me to make an omelet again.

629
00:45:37,251 --> 00:45:39,042
Steven, Steven, wait a second.

630
00:45:42,042 --> 00:45:42,751
What?

631
00:45:43,501 --> 00:45:45,292
You write very well.

632
00:45:46,292 --> 00:45:47,667
You have that potential.

633
00:45:48,959 --> 00:45:53,417
But there is only one problem with your stories.

634
00:45:55,584 --> 00:46:01,126
Just like your name, I see other directors in your stories too.

635
00:46:03,459 --> 00:46:04,709
There is no originality.

636
00:46:07,001 --> 00:46:11,626
Mixing four movies doesn't make a film, Steven.

637
00:46:17,292 --> 00:46:20,709
If you make a movie, it should have your unique mark.

638
00:46:21,709 --> 00:46:27,459
So many people, so many problems,
millions of stories.

639
00:46:29,084 --> 00:46:32,876
Find the story you truly want to tell among them.

640
00:46:44,709 --> 00:46:45,709
Hold on, Dad.

641
00:46:48,001 --> 00:46:50,542
I am studying. Don't keep telling me to study.

642
00:46:50,709 --> 00:46:52,083
Please don't disturb me.

643
00:46:52,084 --> 00:46:55,251
I am studying.
Don't keep irritating me.

644
00:46:59,042 --> 00:47:01,041
I said I am studying, right?
Why are you following me?

645
00:47:01,042 --> 00:47:02,459
Don't torture me.

646
00:47:03,542 --> 00:47:06,416
Go, go, go...

647
00:47:06,417 --> 00:47:08,084
Don't ask me to study so often from now on.

648
00:47:09,084 --> 00:47:09,917
Brother.

649
00:47:10,501 --> 00:47:11,042
Brother.

650
00:47:11,292 --> 00:47:13,333
I haven't opened the shop yet.
Come back after an hour.

651
00:47:13,334 --> 00:47:15,042
Not that, Brother. I need to know something.

652
00:47:15,292 --> 00:47:17,126
Yes? Tell me.

653
00:47:18,001 --> 00:47:18,876
What's wrong with that boy?

654
00:47:19,084 --> 00:47:20,834
He's talking to someone even
though no one is there.

655
00:47:20,959 --> 00:47:24,583
That's a long story. I don't have time to explain now.

656
00:47:24,584 --> 00:47:28,042
Brother, please.
Tell me what happened to him?

657
00:47:30,042 --> 00:47:33,209
He... his father... was my best friend.

658
00:47:34,292 --> 00:47:36,209
He died two years ago.

659
00:47:36,584 --> 00:47:38,751
The boy has no one.
He stays with me.

660
00:47:38,959 --> 00:47:40,501
He was fine for a few days.

661
00:47:41,542 --> 00:47:48,167
Then one day, he suddenly started saying
his father is visible and talking to him.

662
00:47:48,667 --> 00:47:52,334
Since then, everyone calls him crazy.

663
00:47:53,084 --> 00:47:54,834
Do you know what 'crazy' means?

664
00:47:54,959 --> 00:47:56,001
It means mad, right?

665
00:47:57,626 --> 00:47:59,834
Initially, I thought so too, brother.

666
00:48:01,084 --> 00:48:06,042
But slowly, he started telling me
about the transactions between his father and me.

667
00:48:06,584 --> 00:48:10,417
There is no way anyone other than his father
and me could know those things, brother.

668
00:48:10,751 --> 00:48:14,751
If I ask him a question,
he looks to the side and answers.

669
00:48:15,751 --> 00:48:16,584
Just like that.

670
00:48:30,292 --> 00:48:32,501
His father was the one who put him to bed every day.

671
00:48:33,126 --> 00:48:34,709
He woke him up...

672
00:48:37,751 --> 00:48:39,251
and made him study.

673
00:48:41,334 --> 00:48:44,751
His happiness, his pain, everything was his father.

674
00:48:47,959 --> 00:48:50,459
It is true that he can see his father.

675
00:48:51,251 --> 00:48:55,167
If you ask how that is possible,
I don't have an answer, brother.

676
00:48:56,792 --> 00:48:59,126
For those who don't believe, it's a lie.

677
00:49:00,334 --> 00:49:02,959
If you can believe, it's a miracle.

678
00:49:05,126 --> 00:49:05,791
Hey!

679
00:49:05,792 --> 00:49:06,916
Brother, did you bring it?

680
00:49:06,917 --> 00:49:07,958
How long has it been?

681
00:49:07,959 --> 00:49:08,834
We are doing it, brother.

682
00:49:31,959 --> 00:49:32,833
No, no.

683
00:49:32,834 --> 00:49:34,209
Listen to what I say.
- Good morning, sir.

684
00:49:34,501 --> 00:49:36,126
Now we have to finish this schedule within the budget.

685
00:49:38,584 --> 00:49:40,916
Tell the director we must finish within the call sheet.

686
00:49:40,917 --> 00:49:42,166
Make sure the budget doesn't go up.
- Okay Sir.

687
00:49:42,167 --> 00:49:43,459
All of that is your responsibility, alright?
- Okay Sir.

688
00:49:43,876 --> 00:49:44,792
Yes, sir.

689
00:49:47,251 --> 00:49:48,126
Samuel!

690
00:49:50,209 --> 00:49:51,459
Samuel!

691
00:49:54,626 --> 00:49:55,541
Come.

692
00:49:55,542 --> 00:49:56,126
Yes, sir.

693
00:49:58,376 --> 00:50:00,459
Why do you come every day when I said no?

694
00:50:00,792 --> 00:50:03,667
Sir, my name is not Samuel, sir.
It's Steven, sir.

695
00:50:04,417 --> 00:50:05,834
What does the name matter?

696
00:50:06,376 --> 00:50:08,292
There's no creative chip in your brain.

697
00:50:08,792 --> 00:50:10,792
Don't come here unnecessarily and waste your time.

698
00:50:11,376 --> 00:50:12,667
Driver, you go.

699
00:50:13,376 --> 00:50:14,001
Sir...

700
00:50:14,709 --> 00:50:16,792
You too must have faced failures in your career, right, sir?

701
00:50:17,167 --> 00:50:18,292
Did you stop because of that?

702
00:50:19,001 --> 00:50:20,292
Please give me just one opportunity, sir.

703
00:50:20,834 --> 00:50:24,001
If you don't like the story this time,
I won't disturb you again, sir.

704
00:50:26,001 --> 00:50:27,001
Okay.

705
00:50:27,667 --> 00:50:29,166
Come and meet me at the office tomorrow.

706
00:50:29,167 --> 00:50:30,042
Thank you, sir.

707
00:50:30,792 --> 00:50:32,209
Driver, let's go.

708
00:50:37,542 --> 00:50:38,792
Welcome to Sad Party.

709
00:50:38,959 --> 00:50:41,209
What happened, brother?
Hasn't the party started yet?

710
00:50:41,334 --> 00:50:43,584
Party, my foot.
Even the cake cutting hasn't happened yet.

711
00:50:43,751 --> 00:50:45,667
Look, she's sitting over there in the corner.

712
00:50:50,542 --> 00:50:51,459
What happened?

713
00:50:51,709 --> 00:50:53,667
What else? It's about Ajay.

714
00:50:53,959 --> 00:50:56,584
Last year, he came to Chennai just to celebrate her birthday.

715
00:50:56,751 --> 00:50:58,667
This year, apparently he didn't even message her.

716
00:51:02,334 --> 00:51:05,792
With so many people standing around her,
she is only thinking about the one who isn't there.

717
00:51:06,709 --> 00:51:07,959
When will she change?

718
00:51:35,042 --> 00:51:37,167
Pardon my ignorance, but is this some kind of format?

719
00:51:38,042 --> 00:51:38,876
Which one?

720
00:51:39,001 --> 00:51:43,209
After failing in love,
sitting alone like this and staring into space.

721
00:51:47,126 --> 00:51:48,126
No, hear me out.

722
00:51:48,376 --> 00:51:51,000
You loved someone, he left you.

723
00:51:51,001 --> 00:51:52,916
You felt sad about it, it's over, right?

724
00:51:52,917 --> 00:51:54,376
Can't we just move on from that?

725
00:51:56,626 --> 00:51:59,167
Sorry... you continue looking straight.

726
00:52:08,542 --> 00:52:14,667
The first person I ever loved in my life was Ajay.

727
00:52:19,209 --> 00:52:20,251
First love.

728
00:52:22,334 --> 00:52:23,917
If that fails once...

729
00:52:25,459 --> 00:52:26,292
it's hell.

730
00:52:28,709 --> 00:52:31,667
There is purity in first love.

731
00:52:32,251 --> 00:52:33,584
There is honesty.

732
00:52:34,876 --> 00:52:36,917
All the loves that come after that...

733
00:52:37,126 --> 00:52:38,876
If only the first love were real,

734
00:52:39,126 --> 00:52:42,167
then all of our stories should have stopped
at a mother's love, shouldn't they?

735
00:52:49,876 --> 00:52:52,167
Mother is indeed everyone's first love.

736
00:52:56,292 --> 00:52:59,917
There are many great love stories in history.

737
00:53:00,417 --> 00:53:02,001
Not all of them were their first loves, right?

738
00:53:04,167 --> 00:53:08,709
If first love fails, it means the best
love is starting somewhere.

739
00:53:17,542 --> 00:53:22,001
If you sit in one place without moving,
after some time your leg goes numb.

740
00:53:23,459 --> 00:53:24,834
The mind is also like that.

741
00:53:26,876 --> 00:53:28,542
Just try to nudge it.

742
00:53:28,751 --> 00:53:31,792
It will slowly take steps and run on its own.

743
00:54:02,126 --> 00:54:04,666
"Do you remember, do you remember"

744
00:54:04,667 --> 00:54:07,251
"The first rain that soaked you through?"

745
00:54:07,792 --> 00:54:13,167
"Once that rain had passed away,
Did the sky stop existing too?"

746
00:54:13,667 --> 00:54:19,126
"Do you remember, do you remember
The first lamp you ever lit?"

747
00:54:19,376 --> 00:54:24,834
"Once that flame had flickered out,
Did the whole world lose its light?"

748
00:54:25,459 --> 00:54:30,042
"Just seek the joy within the shower,"

749
00:54:31,376 --> 00:54:35,417
"Just find the beauty in the glow."

750
00:54:36,334 --> 00:54:41,751
"Whether it’s the first or the second,
Why does it matter to you so?"

751
00:54:49,876 --> 00:54:56,042
"First love isn’t the ultimate thing, my dear,"

752
00:54:56,917 --> 00:55:03,376
"It never had the power to stop your life."

753
00:55:04,501 --> 00:55:10,626
"First love isn’t the end-all-be-all, my dear,"

754
00:55:11,376 --> 00:55:17,834
"It never had the power to stop your life."

755
00:55:52,001 --> 00:55:54,875
"If you keep looking back,"

756
00:55:54,876 --> 00:56:03,251
"You'll never move forward,
no matter how clear the path."

757
00:56:03,667 --> 00:56:09,209
"If your heart clings to old memories,"

758
00:56:09,584 --> 00:56:14,876
"No celebration can ever bring you new joy."

759
00:56:15,876 --> 00:56:21,084
"Let yesterday's tears flow away,"

760
00:56:21,542 --> 00:56:26,792
"Let fresh songs fill your voice once more."

761
00:56:27,917 --> 00:56:34,084
"First love isn’t the ultimate thing, my dear,"

762
00:56:34,959 --> 00:56:41,417
"It never had the power to stop your life."

763
00:56:42,542 --> 00:56:48,667
"First love isn’t the end-all-be-all, my dear,"

764
00:56:49,417 --> 00:56:55,876
"It never had the power to stop your life."

765
00:57:32,292 --> 00:57:32,917
Hello.

766
00:57:34,834 --> 00:57:35,584
Hello?

767
00:57:37,959 --> 00:57:39,084
Hi Nivi.

768
00:57:39,584 --> 00:57:40,501
How are you?

769
00:57:42,417 --> 00:57:43,584
What do you think?

770
00:57:44,376 --> 00:57:45,459
I'm sorry, Nivi.

771
00:57:45,709 --> 00:57:47,042
Sorry!?

772
00:57:48,959 --> 00:57:51,751
It's so easy for you to just say sorry, isn't it?

773
00:57:53,042 --> 00:57:54,917
Do I look like a fool to you?

774
00:57:55,792 --> 00:57:57,876
Why should I expect anything from you?

775
00:58:00,251 --> 00:58:03,542
Hoping you'll come back someday...
why should I wait?

776
00:58:05,876 --> 00:58:08,376
You left me right before our wedding...

777
00:58:09,084 --> 00:58:11,375
