"It's okay, I will forgive you, won't you come back?"

1073
01:29:19,292 --> 01:29:23,792
"It's okay, I will forgive you, won't you come back?"

1074
01:29:24,792 --> 01:29:26,292
That's not a problem.

1075
01:29:31,084 --> 01:29:32,376
I will talk to you later.

1076
01:29:35,792 --> 01:29:37,209
Is everything okay, Nivi?

1077
01:29:38,167 --> 01:29:39,084
I'm fine.

1078
01:29:39,667 --> 01:29:40,626
No, you are not.

1079
01:29:43,084 --> 01:29:44,376
You are not being normal, Nivi.

1080
01:29:44,792 --> 01:29:48,042
Your'e coming to the office early and stay late,
even after office hours.

1081
01:29:48,584 --> 01:29:50,001
How many days has it been since you last slept?

1082
01:29:50,542 --> 01:29:51,751
Why are you doing all this?

1083
01:29:52,792 --> 01:29:54,167
To forget Steven?

1084
01:29:55,417 --> 01:29:56,751
I can understand your pain.

1085
01:29:56,959 --> 01:29:59,084
It's better if you take a two-month leave.

1086
01:30:00,167 --> 01:30:01,666
Don't worry about your position.

1087
01:30:01,667 --> 01:30:02,667
I will take care of it.

1088
01:30:04,042 --> 01:30:05,126
You deserve a break.

1089
01:30:05,542 --> 01:30:06,542
Please take care.

1090
01:30:11,792 --> 01:30:13,292
Why are you doing all this, Vignesh?

1091
01:30:16,709 --> 01:30:20,042
Just because I'm all alone now, you think
you can take advantage of me, don't you?

1092
01:30:20,292 --> 01:30:21,626
Nivi, what's wrong with you?

1093
01:30:22,001 --> 01:30:22,876
Shut up!

1094
01:30:23,584 --> 01:30:25,501
I clearly know your intentions.

1095
01:30:25,709 --> 01:30:27,209
And how dare you touch me, huh?!

1096
01:30:27,417 --> 01:30:29,667
Nivi, you have completely misunderstood me.
- Just shut up, okay!

1097
01:30:30,042 --> 01:30:32,833
Nivi, what happened?

1098
01:30:32,834 --> 01:30:34,791
Surya, I'm just concerned about her.

1099
01:30:34,792 --> 01:30:36,875
Concern?
Who are you to be concerned about me?

1100
01:30:36,876 --> 01:30:37,292
Nivi!

1101
01:30:37,417 --> 01:30:39,792
And who the hell are you to do favors for me?

1102
01:30:40,042 --> 01:30:41,375
Am I supposed to live on your pity?

1103
01:30:41,376 --> 01:30:42,583
What's wrong with you?

1104
01:30:42,584 --> 01:30:43,792
I don't need your job.

1105
01:30:44,626 --> 01:30:46,333
Nivi, wait. Nivi.

1106
01:30:46,334 --> 01:30:47,334
What's wrong with her, man?
- Nivi!

1107
01:30:54,959 --> 01:30:55,876
Two, two...

1108
01:30:56,917 --> 01:30:57,834
two quarters...

1109
01:30:58,167 --> 01:30:59,626
Brother, get me a full bottle of whisky.

1110
01:31:00,501 --> 01:31:02,834
Look at her, a girl has come to drink alcohol.

1111
01:31:04,542 --> 01:31:05,751
What's it to you if I did? Huh?

1112
01:31:15,292 --> 01:31:17,667
Why are you doing all this?
To forget Steven?

1113
01:31:45,667 --> 01:31:47,083
Hey, did you tell your family before coming?

1114
01:31:47,084 --> 01:31:47,667
Hey, get lost!

1115
01:31:47,876 --> 01:31:49,251
You're insane.
- Go away.

1116
01:32:41,584 --> 01:32:42,334
Get up...

1117
01:32:44,084 --> 01:32:44,834
Get up!

1118
01:32:47,834 --> 01:32:49,667
You said you'd show up at a snap of a finger.

1119
01:32:51,084 --> 01:32:52,917
I need you right now, get up!

1120
01:32:56,459 --> 01:32:57,334
Won't you come?

1121
01:32:59,292 --> 01:33:00,667
You can't come...

1122
01:33:02,834 --> 01:33:06,084
Because you are dead now, you idiot!

1123
01:33:18,751 --> 01:33:19,959
I am crying.

1124
01:33:21,501 --> 01:33:22,626
Can you see it?

1125
01:33:22,917 --> 01:33:24,126
I am crying!

1126
01:33:25,334 --> 01:33:26,626
You scoundrel!

1127
01:33:28,626 --> 01:33:30,292
Why did you even enter my life?

1128
01:33:32,209 --> 01:33:34,751
Mother's love... first love...

1129
01:33:35,292 --> 01:33:37,667
"If first love is lost, the best love comes."

1130
01:33:38,417 --> 01:33:40,042
Who asked you for all this nonsense?!

1131
01:33:42,417 --> 01:33:45,209
Do you think you’re some social reformer
like Kandukuri Veeresalingam?

1132
01:33:48,209 --> 01:33:50,834
You're just a writer who lives off
writing shallow love stories...

1133
01:33:53,001 --> 01:33:54,501
Steven Shankar!

1134
01:33:59,167 --> 01:34:02,251
Will anyone even love you, huh?

1135
01:34:03,209 --> 01:34:03,834
Huh?!

1136
01:34:13,126 --> 01:34:14,417
But I loved you.

1137
01:34:37,959 --> 01:34:39,626
I loved you with all my heart.

1138
01:34:43,167 --> 01:34:49,251
In a world where people abandon the woman
they've loved for years at the wedding altar...

1139
01:34:53,417 --> 01:34:57,209
For a small help I did...

1140
01:35:00,376 --> 01:35:01,917
you made me feel like a goddess.

1141
01:35:04,834 --> 01:35:07,334
If one is born to truly wonderful parents,

1142
01:35:09,042 --> 01:35:11,084
one inherits that very same good heart.

1143
01:35:13,709 --> 01:35:15,667
A love that only knows how to give,

1144
01:35:19,501 --> 01:35:21,167
Love that expects nothing in return...

1145
01:35:24,917 --> 01:35:33,584
Who else can teach how to love
a person better than you?!

1146
01:35:37,042 --> 01:35:38,459
I need you...

1147
01:35:40,334 --> 01:35:41,917
You’re a Treasure!

1148
01:35:42,292 --> 01:35:44,001
I need you!

1149
01:35:44,501 --> 01:35:46,042
Can you hear me?

1150
01:35:47,584 --> 01:35:48,834
I am calling out to you!

1151
01:35:51,751 --> 01:35:52,834
At least you come…

1152
01:35:54,084 --> 01:35:56,459
or take me along with you.

1153
01:35:57,417 --> 01:35:58,417
Wake up.

1154
01:36:08,001 --> 01:36:10,251
If you truly can't stand seeing my tears...

1155
01:36:11,292 --> 01:36:12,251
Come...

1156
01:36:14,792 --> 01:36:18,167
If you have a love that cannot
let go of me, then come.

1157
01:36:24,459 --> 01:36:26,167
Come... Steven...

1158
01:36:26,751 --> 01:36:27,709
Come...

1159
01:38:34,917 --> 01:38:37,376
Did it take you this long to call me?

1160
01:38:39,334 --> 01:38:40,334
How have you been?

1161
01:39:11,042 --> 01:39:12,417
Why are you running away looking at me?

1162
01:39:30,167 --> 01:39:31,042
Steven...

1163
01:39:31,751 --> 01:39:32,667
Yes, it's Steven.

1164
01:39:33,126 --> 01:39:34,042
Didn't I tell you?

1165
01:39:34,209 --> 01:39:35,709
You just have to call me with love...

1166
01:39:36,042 --> 01:39:38,626
and I'll fly to you from wherever I am.

1167
01:39:46,334 --> 01:39:47,292
I've come back.

1168
01:39:47,417 --> 01:39:48,626
You have nothing to worry about anymore.

1169
01:39:54,251 --> 01:39:55,001
Steven...

1170
01:40:03,834 --> 01:40:05,126
You cannot touch me.

1171
01:40:20,709 --> 01:40:24,834
Hey, is there some problem?

1172
01:40:25,501 --> 01:40:27,251
What are you doing down on
the road all alone?

1173
01:40:30,001 --> 01:40:32,292
No one but you will be able to see me.

1174
01:40:37,917 --> 01:40:40,626
She looks crazy.
Why should we get involved?

1175
01:41:15,334 --> 01:41:16,626
Is all this real, Steven?

1176
01:41:16,876 --> 01:41:17,626
It is real.

1177
01:41:19,542 --> 01:41:20,875
Did you come back just for me?

1178
01:41:20,876 --> 01:41:22,334
I came back only for you.

1179
01:41:24,917 --> 01:41:25,959
Will you stay with me now?

1180
01:41:26,334 --> 01:41:27,542
I will stay with you.

1181
01:41:28,292 --> 01:41:29,208
Life long?

1182
01:41:29,209 --> 01:41:30,167
Life long.

1183
01:41:36,209 --> 01:41:37,584
I can't believe this, Steven.

1184
01:41:39,376 --> 01:41:41,584
Does this ever happen anywhere?

1185
01:41:41,959 --> 01:41:45,626
Even history would not like,
if all the love stories were the same.

1186
01:42:22,709 --> 01:42:26,876
"No matter what anyone says,
or what they might think.."

1187
01:42:27,292 --> 01:42:31,209
"Our world is ours alone, isn't it?"

1188
01:42:31,792 --> 01:42:35,709
"No matter where the horizons fade,
or what becomes of the stars,"

1189
01:42:36,376 --> 01:42:40,334
"As long as you are by my side, nothing else matters."

1190
01:42:40,542 --> 01:42:45,501
"Wherever life leads,
won't I always be joined with you?"

1191
01:42:58,084 --> 01:43:02,167
"Like gentle, soothing waves...
like a dream beyond all senses..."

1192
01:43:02,584 --> 01:43:06,542
"Our story has begun once again, just like this."

1193
01:43:29,334 --> 01:43:29,917
Nivi!

1194
01:43:32,042 --> 01:43:34,084
What happened?
- Mosquito!

1195
01:43:35,376 --> 01:43:39,584
"This tiny heart of mine wants
to skip and dance,"

1196
01:43:39,917 --> 01:43:44,042
"Like a little fledgling,
it wants to spread its wings."

1197
01:43:44,542 --> 01:43:45,166
When?

1198
01:43:45,167 --> 01:43:47,750
"The games we once played at school,
the songs we sang at the temple.."

1199
01:43:47,751 --> 01:43:48,500
"Why?"

1200
01:43:48,501 --> 01:43:51,250
For some reason, today,
my heart wants to play and sing them all with you.

1201
01:43:51,251 --> 01:43:58,876
"The way you’ve changed...
wow, it’s truly wonderful!"

1202
01:43:59,751 --> 01:44:05,292
"No one could ever share moments
the way we do."

1203
01:44:18,251 --> 01:44:22,334
"Like gentle, soothing waves...
like a dream beyond all senses..."

1204
01:44:22,751 --> 01:44:26,709
"Our story has begun once again, just like this."

1205
01:44:31,626 --> 01:44:32,584
He's there.

1206
01:44:34,376 --> 01:44:37,209
Who?
- Hero, he's alive

1207
01:44:56,417 --> 01:45:00,501
"This story hasn't been printed in any books,"

1208
01:45:01,001 --> 01:45:05,125
"Nor does it seem to have ever
graced the silver screen."

1209
01:45:05,126 --> 01:45:08,792
"This tale that you and I write
in our solitude feels so brand new;"

1210
01:45:08,917 --> 01:45:12,167
"I swear, not a single soul would
believe that such a fate could be written."

1211
01:45:12,292 --> 01:45:15,459
And yet... it’s beautiful...

1212
01:45:16,709 --> 01:45:19,584
"it’s so very beautiful."

1213
01:45:20,876 --> 01:45:26,126
"If every love were just the same,
History would never remember it."

1214
01:45:39,292 --> 01:45:43,376
"Like gentle, soothing waves...
like a dream beyond all senses..."

1215
01:45:43,792 --> 01:45:47,751
"Our story has begun once again, just like this."

1216
01:45:52,792 --> 01:45:53,583
You got caught.

1217
01:45:53,584 --> 01:45:55,167
Talk softly on the phone and walk away.

1218
01:45:57,417 --> 01:45:58,167
Hello, mom

1219
01:45:58,959 --> 01:46:00,126
Earphones...

1220
01:46:05,667 --> 01:46:07,084
What's wrong with her these days?

1221
01:46:07,459 --> 01:46:08,876
I don't understand either.

1222
01:46:09,042 --> 01:46:12,501
The other day too, she was laughing
loudly while talking on the phone.

1223
01:46:12,626 --> 01:46:13,959
She stopped as soon as she saw me.

1224
01:46:15,209 --> 01:46:17,208
She was so dull just a week ago.

1225
01:46:17,209 --> 01:46:18,833
Why this sudden changeover now?

1226
01:46:18,834 --> 01:46:19,876
It's all because I came, right?

1227
01:46:20,042 --> 01:46:21,959
What change? She just forgot Steven.

1228
01:46:23,792 --> 01:46:25,126
What are you talking about, man?

1229
01:46:25,376 --> 01:46:26,459
Don't you get it?

1230
01:46:26,959 --> 01:46:29,251
She came out of
the grief of losing him.

1231
01:46:29,501 --> 01:46:31,126
What, so quickly?

1232
01:46:31,417 --> 01:46:32,292
What's quick about it?

1233
01:46:32,709 --> 01:46:34,792
Don't we move on? She did the same.

1234
01:46:35,542 --> 01:46:38,292
We are different.
She loved Steven, didn't she?

1235
01:46:38,501 --> 01:46:39,501
That's true.

1236
01:46:39,792 --> 01:46:41,667
Oh, whatever.
As if that was a great love story!

1237
01:46:41,917 --> 01:46:45,959
Ajay's was a three-year love,
so she was in depression for four months.

1238
01:46:46,751 --> 01:46:49,417
What is this Steven's?
Ten days at most.

1239
01:46:50,542 --> 01:46:51,959
It's expired, bro.

1240
01:47:00,334 --> 01:47:01,292
Sorry.. sorry.

1241
01:47:02,709 --> 01:47:05,626
So you find it funny to call
Steven's love trivial, huh?

1242
01:47:06,084 --> 01:47:08,626
Hey, they don't know what's happening here.

1243
01:47:08,834 --> 01:47:10,166
They said it out of ignorance.
Let it go.

1244
01:47:10,167 --> 01:47:11,251
No, I won't.

1245
01:47:11,626 --> 01:47:14,209
You must come and prove that
Steven's is a great love story.

1246
01:47:14,376 --> 01:47:16,751
Hey, why do we need to prove
anything to them, Steven?

1247
01:47:17,126 --> 01:47:19,209
I need to.
Are you coming or not?

1248
01:47:20,459 --> 01:47:22,459
Okay, I'll come.
What should I say?

1249
01:47:24,751 --> 01:47:26,292
That's better.

1250
01:47:26,709 --> 01:47:27,834
Now leave it to me.

1251
01:47:29,001 --> 01:47:31,917
This Sequence Is Written and
directed by Steven Shankar!

1252
01:47:35,667 --> 01:47:37,876
I heard what you guys were talking
about when I was in the room.

1253
01:47:39,626 --> 01:47:41,167
I haven't forgotten Steven.

1254
01:47:41,917 --> 01:47:43,542
I will never forget him.

1255
01:47:45,626 --> 01:47:49,292
If anyone speaks ill of Steven once more...

1256
01:47:50,376 --> 01:47:51,167
it won't end well for you.

1257
01:47:57,251 --> 01:48:00,167
Nivi, why are you yelling at us about this now?

1258
01:48:00,501 --> 01:48:02,000
I said you forgot Steven.

1259
01:48:02,001 --> 01:48:03,834
Isn't forgetting a good thing?
Move on.

1260
01:48:05,417 --> 01:48:07,084
Steven, Steven... you keep nagging.

1261
01:48:07,417 --> 01:48:09,042
As if you've known him for ten years.

1262
01:48:11,334 --> 01:48:14,501
There's sambar there, right?
Throw it on his face.

1263
01:48:15,584 --> 01:48:17,542
An actor must do what the director says. Go!

1264
01:48:27,376 --> 01:48:27,917
Ahhh!

1265
01:48:30,959 --> 01:48:33,042
Whatever I say, repeat it without asking why.

1266
01:48:34,876 --> 01:48:36,084
Steven is my world.

1267
01:48:36,459 --> 01:48:37,583
Steven is my world.

1268
01:48:37,584 --> 01:48:38,876
Steven is my life.

1269
01:48:39,001 --> 01:48:40,501
Steven is my life.

1270
01:48:40,876 --> 01:48:44,209
Even more than Ajay,
I like Steven very, very, very much.

1271
01:48:47,376 --> 01:48:48,334
You have to say it.

1272
01:48:50,792 --> 01:48:54,126
Even more than Ajay,
I like Steven very, very much.

1273
01:48:54,334 --> 01:48:55,376
You missed one 'very'.

1274
01:48:57,167 --> 01:48:59,126
I like Steven very, very, very much.

1275
01:49:02,626 --> 01:49:04,209
Is my love a joke to you?

1276
01:49:13,459 --> 01:49:14,834
Why did you bring up Ajay now?

1277
01:49:16,501 --> 01:49:18,626
Because I love you more than he ever could.

1278
01:49:19,334 --> 01:49:21,334
Because I believe that you love me more, too.

1279
01:49:21,584 --> 01:49:23,584
And because I want everyone to know
that, not just the two of us.

1280
01:49:34,126 --> 01:49:35,417
Why are you so angry, Steven?

1281
01:49:37,542 --> 01:49:38,209
Tell me, what happened?

1282
01:49:41,792 --> 01:49:45,042
Most people want to be remembered
for generations after they’re gone.

1283
01:49:46,584 --> 01:49:49,584
But our people… they forgot me in just a few days.

1284
01:49:52,876 --> 01:49:53,667
It’s not their fault, really.

1285
01:49:54,292 --> 01:49:57,459
I’m just an orphan;
who would bother to remember me?

1286
01:49:58,084 --> 01:50:00,084
Besides, it’s not like I accomplished
anything of value while I was alive.

1287
01:50:08,126 --> 01:50:12,709
I used to dream of seeing my name up
there on a 70mm cinema screen.

1288
01:50:15,001 --> 01:50:17,001
I wanted to create an identity of my own.

1289
01:50:18,542 --> 01:50:19,334
but none of it ever happened.

1290
01:50:21,626 --> 01:50:22,876
I’m a failure, Nivi.

1291
01:50:24,917 --> 01:50:28,292
Steven Shankar’s life is nothing more
than a piece of scrap paper.

1292
01:50:31,959 --> 01:50:33,167
The strange thing is,

1293
01:50:33,876 --> 01:50:35,876
I didn’t have any of these
regrets in the moments before I died.

1294
01:50:38,334 --> 01:50:39,501
You know how they say...

1295
01:50:40,459 --> 01:50:44,751
your whole life flashes before
your eyes in those final seconds?

1296
01:50:46,626 --> 01:50:47,792
Do you know what I saw?

1297
01:50:50,001 --> 01:50:51,667
I saw the last six months I spent with all of you.

1298
01:50:58,251 --> 01:50:59,792
I don't know why or how,

1299
01:51:00,709 --> 01:51:02,376
but I’ve been given this second
chance to be with you again.

1300
01:51:03,584 --> 01:51:07,167
My only fear is that you'll listen to what
they're saying and change your mind about me.

1301
01:51:09,584 --> 01:51:10,542
That’s why I’m so angry.

1302
01:51:13,542 --> 01:51:14,709
Let’s do this, Steven.

1303
01:51:17,376 --> 01:51:20,709
It’s getting a bit difficult staying here anyway.

1304
01:51:24,292 --> 01:51:25,834
How about we move to a new house?

1305
01:51:29,751 --> 01:51:32,126
Just you and me.

1306
01:51:33,751 --> 01:51:34,626
No one else.

1307
01:51:38,626 --> 01:51:39,376
Really?

1308
01:51:40,126 --> 01:51:40,626
Yes.

1309
01:52:17,042 --> 01:52:19,001
You should've seen Chaitu's face

1310
01:52:19,292 --> 01:52:20,458
It's so miserable.

1311
01:52:20,459 --> 01:52:21,542
Didn't I tell you...
- Excuse me...

1312
01:52:23,167 --> 01:52:24,292
Can I take this chair?

1313
01:52:24,417 --> 01:52:25,417
No, he's there.

1314
01:52:27,042 --> 01:52:27,584
Who?

1315
01:52:28,292 --> 01:52:30,084
I mean.. he's coming.

1316
01:52:35,792 --> 01:52:37,376
Excuse me, you're Nivi, right?

1317
01:52:41,542 --> 01:52:42,126
Yeah.

1318
01:52:42,334 --> 01:52:42,709
You..?

1319
01:52:42,834 --> 01:52:44,251
Hi! I'm Jyo.

1320
01:52:45,959 --> 01:52:46,501
Hi!

1321
01:52:48,376 --> 01:52:50,751
You probably don't know me,
but I've heard a lot about you.

1322
01:52:50,917 --> 01:52:52,501
Ajay talks about you all the time.

1323
01:52:55,334 --> 01:52:55,709
Oh!

1324
01:52:56,417 --> 01:52:57,042
Hi!

1325
01:52:57,626 --> 01:52:59,501
Are you here in Chennai on a trip?

1326
01:52:59,792 --> 01:53:00,501
No, actually.

1327
01:53:01,084 --> 01:53:04,042
Our entire team moved from
Bangalore to Chennai three months ago.

1328
01:53:04,501 --> 01:53:05,292
Ajay moved too.

1329
01:53:09,459 --> 01:53:10,042
Oh, really?

1330
01:53:10,876 --> 01:53:11,667
I had no idea.

1331
01:53:12,876 --> 01:53:14,084
Yeah, the Guindy branch.

1332
01:53:14,292 --> 01:53:17,084
He's still at the office.
I just came out to meet my friends

1333
01:53:18,792 --> 01:53:19,250
Okay.

1334
01:53:19,251 --> 01:53:20,001
Okay, let's go.

1335
01:53:22,667 --> 01:53:24,376
Okay, nice meeting you.

1336
01:53:24,626 --> 01:53:25,126
Bye!

1337
01:53:25,417 --> 01:53:25,875
Okay.

1338
01:53:25,876 --> 01:53:26,334
Bye!

1339
01:53:27,126 --> 01:53:29,876
Oh, and by the way, congratulations.

1340
01:53:30,251 --> 01:53:31,584
I'm really happy for you and Ajay.

1341
01:53:32,876 --> 01:53:33,417
Wait, for what?

1342
01:53:34,126 --> 01:53:35,376
Your relationship!

1343
01:53:36,876 --> 01:53:39,626
What relationship?
Ajay and I are just friends.

1344
01:53:42,126 --> 01:53:44,751
Who told you we were together?

1345
01:53:47,542 --> 01:53:48,291
Well...

1346
01:53:48,292 --> 01:53:49,209
Are you coming or not?

1347
01:53:52,292 --> 01:53:53,709
Sorry, my bad.

1348
01:53:54,376 --> 01:53:55,292
I must've gotten it wrong.

1349
01:53:55,751 --> 01:53:56,792
Just a little misunderstanding.

1350
01:53:57,126 --> 01:53:57,751
Bye!

1351
01:54:06,001 --> 01:54:07,792
Why did you talk to her instead of just walking away?

1352
01:54:09,542 --> 01:54:11,666
Hey! I didn't start the conversation.
She came up and spoke to me.

1353
01:54:11,667 --> 01:54:12,709
How is that my fault?

1354
01:54:13,126 --> 01:54:14,792
No. You shouldn't have brought up Ajay.

1355
01:54:15,167 --> 01:54:16,209
Do you think she'll keep quiet now?

1356
01:54:16,667 --> 01:54:18,209
She'll definitely tell Ajay about this.

1357
01:54:18,709 --> 01:54:20,459
And he'll definitely want to talk to you.

1358
01:54:20,917 --> 01:54:22,542
He'll find a way to meet you.

1359
01:54:22,959 --> 01:54:25,709
If my guess is right... he'll definitely call you.

1360
01:54:25,876 --> 01:54:28,376
Somehow, he'll find a way to reach you.
I know he will.

1361
01:54:29,251 --> 01:54:32,501
For your kind information,
I blocked Ajay a long time ago.

1362
01:54:34,501 --> 01:54:36,333
Fine, you've blocked him on your phone...
but what if he comes to your house?

1363
01:54:36,334 --> 01:54:38,334
Why would he, Steven?
He doesn't even know my address.

1364
01:54:38,876 --> 01:54:39,917
What if our friends tells him?

1365
01:54:40,417 --> 01:54:43,375
Why would they?
Why are you overthinking this?

1366
01:54:43,376 --> 01:54:45,709
No... Siri can't keep a secret.
She'll blurt it out if anyone asks.

1367
01:54:47,376 --> 01:54:48,917
So what do you want me to do now?

1368
01:54:49,126 --> 01:54:49,876
Call Siri.

1369
01:54:50,834 --> 01:54:51,501
Go ahead, call her!

1370
01:54:55,209 --> 01:54:56,501
Put it on speaker... Turn on the speaker.

1371
01:54:56,876 --> 01:54:57,459
Speaker...

1372
01:55:01,167 --> 01:55:01,917
Yeah, tell me.

1373
01:55:02,584 --> 01:55:03,917
Did Ajay call you?

1374
01:55:04,084 --> 01:55:05,876
Ajay? Why would he call me?

1375
01:55:07,042 --> 01:55:10,792
If he does... don't tell him my new address.

1376
01:55:11,667 --> 01:55:13,458
Nivi... did you meet Ajay?

1377
01:55:13,459 --> 01:55:16,459
Hey! Don't tell her anything else.
Hang up! Hang up, I'm telling you!

1378
01:55:19,209 --> 01:55:20,209
What's wrong with her?

1379
01:55:20,792 --> 01:55:22,042
What's wrong with you, Steven?

1380
01:55:22,376 --> 01:55:23,751
Why are you being so hysterical?

1381
01:55:25,209 --> 01:55:25,917
What's wrong with me?

1382
01:55:26,751 --> 01:55:27,459
I'm fine.

1383
01:55:28,167 --> 01:55:29,042
Nothing's wrong with me.

1384
01:55:30,542 --> 01:55:32,459
Why would anything be wrong?
I'm fine... I'm perfectly fine.

1385
01:55:32,876 --> 01:55:34,001
I'm fine... I'm perfectly fine.

1386
01:55:36,459 --> 01:55:37,334
He's here.

1387
01:55:38,959 --> 01:55:40,541
Didn't I tell you?
Didn't I say he'd come?

1388
01:55:40,542 --> 01:55:42,166
She must've called him, and he's come back.

1389
01:55:42,167 --> 01:55:44,417
Let's see how he gets inside.
Let's see how he gets in!

1390
01:55:57,209 --> 01:55:58,792
Hello, What happened?

1391
01:55:59,834 --> 01:56:01,209
Looks like you ordered some food.

1392
01:56:01,334 --> 01:56:02,626
It's here. Go and eat.

1393
01:56:05,834 --> 01:56:07,542
Freshen up, eat something, and get some rest.

1394
01:56:08,001 --> 01:56:09,626
Don't think about anything else.

1395
01:56:25,376 --> 01:56:26,334
What’s wrong?

1396
01:56:26,959 --> 01:56:28,084
Can’t sleep?

1397
01:56:28,626 --> 01:56:30,209
Are you thinking about Ajay?

1398
01:56:32,209 --> 01:56:33,667
It's nothing like that, Steven.

1399
01:56:36,542 --> 01:56:38,292
Alright then, go back to sleep.

1400
01:56:40,542 --> 01:56:42,126
Goodnight. Sorry for bothering you.

1401
01:56:44,292 --> 01:56:45,084
Steven...

1402
01:56:49,626 --> 01:56:50,959
what do you think happened between them?

1403
01:56:55,626 --> 01:56:58,251
If they just broke up because it didn't work out,

1404
01:56:59,792 --> 01:57:03,417
then why did she act like nothing
was wrong when she was with me?

1405
01:57:05,084 --> 01:57:07,459
If there really was nothing between them,

1406
01:57:08,501 --> 01:57:13,209
then why did Ajay use Jyo's name
as an excuse to break up with me?

1407
01:57:14,126 --> 01:57:17,126
And why is Ajay here in Chennai?

1408
01:57:18,917 --> 01:57:21,542
I feel so clueless about everything.

1409
01:57:26,584 --> 01:57:27,626
Don’t look at me like that.

1410
01:57:28,459 --> 01:57:30,209
It’s not that I still have feelings for Ajay.

1411
01:57:30,834 --> 01:57:33,542
He is definitely a closed chapter in my life.

1412
01:57:34,709 --> 01:57:38,667
I’m just curious about one part of the story
that I don’t understand, that’s all.

1413
01:57:41,917 --> 01:57:42,709
Fine then!

1414
01:57:43,001 --> 01:57:44,667
Go ahead, find that chapter and read it.

1415
01:57:45,042 --> 01:57:47,084
Steven, wait... I just wanted to know, that's all.

1416
01:57:47,251 --> 01:57:48,417
Did I say you couldn't?

1417
01:57:48,667 --> 01:57:49,959
Go ahead, unblock his number and talk to him!

1418
01:57:50,209 --> 01:57:51,041
Steven, I'm sorry...

1419
01:57:51,042 --> 01:57:54,167
I don't want to know about it, okay?
- Save your apology. I don't need it.

1420
01:58:06,126 --> 01:58:07,042
Hello...
- Yeah, tell me.

1421
01:58:07,209 --> 01:58:08,542
Can we meet once?

1422
01:58:09,251 --> 01:58:11,251
Siri, I’m really not in the mood
to see anyone right now, please.

1423
01:58:11,626 --> 01:58:13,791
No, listen to what I’m saying for a second...

1424
01:58:13,792 --> 01:58:16,376
Siri, please understand.
I’m just not in the mood to meet.

1425
01:58:16,584 --> 01:58:17,751
Bye.
- Hello? Hello!

1426
01:58:18,626 --> 01:58:19,167
What was that?

1427
01:58:19,417 --> 01:58:20,459
Did Ajay call Siri?

1428
01:58:21,001 --> 01:58:22,042
Does he want to talk to you?

1429
01:58:22,959 --> 01:58:23,834
Does he want to meet?

1430
01:58:24,167 --> 01:58:25,791
Is she trying to play mediator now?

1431
01:58:25,792 --> 01:58:27,667
Steven, don't start this again, please.

1432
01:58:27,917 --> 01:58:29,459
No, I heard you. You’re lying to me.

1433
01:58:29,584 --> 01:58:30,916
I heard you say you weren’t in the mood to meet.

1434
01:58:30,917 --> 01:58:32,626
She was talking about Murugan’s mother.

1435
01:58:34,126 --> 01:58:35,542
She wants to meet me.

1436
01:58:37,001 --> 01:58:37,751
Who is Murugan?

1437
01:58:38,501 --> 01:58:40,042
The boy you saved in that accident.

1438
01:58:41,126 --> 01:58:42,084
I don't know why...

1439
01:58:42,959 --> 01:58:46,001
But his mother has been wanting
to meet me for a long time.

1440
01:58:51,459 --> 01:58:53,541
I was just wondering what
she’d want to talk about...

1441
01:58:53,542 --> 01:58:54,042
Let’s go meet her.

1442
01:58:56,709 --> 01:58:57,251
Please.

1443
01:58:58,084 --> 01:58:59,167
Why now, Steven?

1444
01:58:59,834 --> 01:59:01,126
I want to see him.

1445
01:59:01,917 --> 01:59:02,792
Let’s go, please.

1446
01:59:10,417 --> 01:59:11,167
Come in, dear!

1447
01:59:12,376 --> 01:59:13,292
Come, have a seat.

1448
01:59:13,626 --> 01:59:15,042
It’s alright, Auntie.

1449
01:59:15,251 --> 01:59:16,417
Please sit down, dear.

1450
01:59:16,667 --> 01:59:17,667
Will you have a cold drink?

1451
01:59:17,876 --> 01:59:18,834
Oh, no thank you, Auntie.

1452
01:59:19,167 --> 01:59:20,417
It’s no trouble, please have one.

1453
01:59:20,709 --> 01:59:21,459
Hey, Murugan!

1454
01:59:21,626 --> 01:59:22,291
Mom!

1455
01:59:22,292 --> 01:59:22,959
Come here.

1456
01:59:24,334 --> 01:59:25,709
Look, sister is here!

1457
01:59:29,292 --> 01:59:31,084
Here, take this and go get us
some cold drinks from the shop.

1458
01:59:37,834 --> 01:59:41,167
I’ve wanted to meet you for so long
and talk to you, dear.

1459
01:59:41,626 --> 01:59:45,084
But now that you’re finally here,
I’m at a loss for words.

1460
01:59:46,376 --> 01:59:48,376
It's okay, Auntie.
Please talk to me.

1461
01:59:52,001 --> 01:59:57,667
Ever since that accident,
that boy has never left my thoughts.

1462
02:00:03,792 --> 02:00:08,376
When someone leaves the house saying they
will be right back, and then never returns...

1463
02:00:08,709 --> 02:00:12,334
I know exactly how agonizing that pain is, dear.

1464
02:00:14,501 --> 02:00:19,667
Five years ago, his father went out to hunt one day...

1465
02:00:21,501 --> 02:00:22,834
and came back as a corpse.

1466
02:00:28,376 --> 02:00:31,792
My son is all I have left.

1467
02:00:34,001 --> 02:00:35,417
He is my entire world.

1468
02:00:37,209 --> 02:00:43,292
Tell me, how can I ever repay the
boy who saved him?

1469
02:00:47,376 --> 02:00:50,376
Words can’t describe what he means to me.

1470
02:00:51,376 --> 02:00:53,376
But I want to show you something.

1471
02:00:53,709 --> 02:00:55,667
Come with me, dear...

1472
02:00:58,376 --> 02:00:59,417
Come dear... come

1473
02:01:00,667 --> 02:01:02,126
look at this.

1474
02:01:02,251 --> 02:01:04,251
Auntie! What have you done?!

1475
02:01:05,334 --> 02:01:06,542
What's wrong with it, dear?

1476
02:01:20,209 --> 02:01:24,959
We pray to God for His blessings, never
knowing whether He'll grant us what we ask for.

1477
02:01:25,584 --> 02:01:26,751
We pray to God for boons.

1478
02:01:27,959 --> 02:01:35,709
But this boy, without even knowing who we were,
put his own life on the line to save my son.

1479
02:01:36,417 --> 02:01:39,292
That's why I regard him as God.

1480
02:01:47,626 --> 02:01:53,751
When people ask who saved my son,
I tell them it was God.

1481
02:01:56,792 --> 02:01:59,292
Auntie, his name is Steven.

1482
02:02:00,251 --> 02:02:03,042
To all of you, his name might be Steven,

1483
02:02:04,292 --> 02:02:05,876
but to me, he is truly God.

1484
02:02:15,501 --> 02:02:17,709
Steven, what’s your real name?

1485
02:02:18,709 --> 02:02:19,417
Devudu (God).

1486
02:02:33,417 --> 02:02:35,333
I remember someone once telling me
that no one would value their death,

1487
02:02:35,334 --> 02:02:37,084
that their life was just a piece of scrap paper.

1488
02:02:37,459 --> 02:02:42,376
But look at that woman...
she’s worshipping you as if you were divine.

1489
02:02:49,001 --> 02:02:50,209
Why don't you say anything?

1490
02:02:51,792 --> 02:02:55,542
Ever since she spoke those words, I’ve been speechless.

1491
02:02:57,584 --> 02:02:59,251
My hollow heart feels full again.

1492
02:03:00,042 --> 02:03:02,251
For a moment, I truly felt like I'm born again.

1493
02:03:05,084 --> 02:03:05,751
Steven...

1494
02:03:07,959 --> 02:03:09,417
since you're 'God' now,

1495
02:03:12,042 --> 02:03:14,501
would you grant me a wish if I asked?

1496
02:03:17,334 --> 02:03:18,209
Go ahead and ask.

1497
02:03:21,959 --> 02:03:25,709
Will you come back to life...
just for a moment, for me?

1498
02:03:28,834 --> 02:03:29,709
What if I do?

1499
02:03:30,751 --> 02:03:32,751
I want to touch you... just once.

1500
02:03:34,876 --> 02:03:35,417
And then?

1501
02:03:37,876 --> 02:03:40,834
I want to embrace you tightly...

1502
02:03:42,292 --> 02:03:43,376
until my heart's content.

1503
02:03:45,084 --> 02:03:45,626
And then?

1504
02:03:48,417 --> 02:03:50,251
I want to kiss you...

1505
02:03:52,334 --> 02:03:53,751
in a way I'll never forget, Steven.

1506
02:03:57,251 --> 02:03:58,084
Your wish is granted.

1507
02:04:23,209 --> 02:04:23,834
Let's forget about that wish...

1508
02:04:25,292 --> 02:04:26,834
it’ll only bring more pain later on.

1509
02:04:33,709 --> 02:04:35,126
If there are any wishes to be fulfilled, please ask.

1510
02:04:36,209 --> 02:04:37,251
What else could I possibly want?

1511
02:04:39,376 --> 02:04:40,209
Give him a call.

1512
02:04:42,751 --> 02:04:43,334
What?

1513
02:04:44,792 --> 02:04:48,334
You said you were curious, didn't you?

1514
02:04:48,917 --> 02:04:49,792
Go on, call him.

1515
02:04:51,667 --> 02:04:52,376
You want me to call Ajay?

1516
02:04:52,709 --> 02:04:53,292
Yes, him.

1517
02:04:53,917 --> 02:04:58,292
You want me to unblock Ajay and call him?

1518
02:04:58,709 --> 02:05:01,417
Don't overthink it, or I might have
to take back that boon I just gave you.

1519
02:05:03,084 --> 02:05:04,209
Do you want it on speaker?

1520
02:05:04,501 --> 02:05:05,876
No need. Go ahead.

1521
02:05:07,167 --> 02:05:07,876
Hello!
- Hello!

1522
02:05:08,001 --> 02:05:09,126
Hi Nivi!
- Hi Ajay!

1523
02:05:09,376 --> 02:05:10,375
I met Jyo today.

1524
02:05:10,376 --> 02:05:11,416
Well...
- Yeah!

1525
02:05:11,417 --> 02:05:13,250
I need to talk to you about that.

1526
02:05:13,251 --> 02:05:13,709
Okay.

1527
02:05:14,126 --> 02:05:14,501
Sure.

1528
02:05:15,334 --> 02:05:16,126
Can we meet tomorrow?

1529
02:05:16,709 --> 02:05:17,958
Tomorrow?
- Yeah.

1530
02:05:17,959 --> 02:05:18,709
Okay.

1531
02:05:19,626 --> 02:05:20,667
Hello, Nivi?

1532
02:05:20,834 --> 02:05:22,916
Yeah, I’ll let you know the time and place.

1533
02:05:22,917 --> 02:05:24,126
Bye.
- Okay, bye.

1534
02:05:25,501 --> 02:05:26,084
What's wrong?

1535
02:05:26,501 --> 02:05:27,542
Why did you say you’d meet him?

1536
02:05:28,126 --> 02:05:30,542
Well, if I want to know about it,
I'll have to meet him, won't I?

1537
02:05:30,709 --> 02:05:31,709
You could have just asked him
over the phone!

1538
02:05:33,001 --> 02:05:33,459
Sorry.

1539
02:05:34,167 --> 02:05:35,501
Should I cancel?
I'll call him back and tell him I can't.

1540
02:05:35,667 --> 02:05:36,167
Hello.

1541
02:05:36,501 --> 02:05:37,042
Forget it.

1542
02:05:37,292 --> 02:05:39,751
This is why God stopped granting boons.

1543
02:06:05,626 --> 02:06:06,501
How have you been, Nivi?

1544
02:06:07,792 --> 02:06:08,376
I’m good.

1545
02:06:12,001 --> 02:06:12,709
How’s work going?

1546
02:06:13,626 --> 02:06:14,501
I resigned.

1547
02:06:14,792 --> 02:06:16,084
I’m looking for something else now.

1548
02:06:17,001 --> 02:06:17,751
What happened?

1549
02:06:20,876 --> 02:06:21,501
Ajay,

1550
02:06:22,376 --> 02:06:25,126
let's put that aside and talk
about what really matters.

1551
02:06:28,001 --> 02:06:31,084
What you told me at the railway station...

1552
02:06:31,459 --> 02:06:34,376
and what Jyo told me today don't match at all.

1553
02:06:35,042 --> 02:06:36,084
What’s going on?

1554
02:06:38,001 --> 02:06:39,709
I didn't tell Jyo any of that, Nivi.

1555
02:06:42,334 --> 02:06:45,667
I just didn't feel right about the whole situation.

1556
02:06:47,417 --> 02:06:50,417
Like you said, I think I was just confused.

1557
02:06:52,667 --> 02:06:54,334
At the same time, when marriage
with you came up,

1558
02:06:54,834 --> 02:06:56,251
I didn't know what to do.

1559
02:06:57,459 --> 02:07:00,876
I couldn't see any other option but to call it off.

1560
02:07:02,251 --> 02:07:04,167
But after I left you at the station that day,

1561
02:07:05,001 --> 02:07:06,751
every single moment we spent together
started flashing through my mind.

1562
02:07:07,792 --> 02:07:10,834
How we met, how we fell in love...

1563
02:07:11,459 --> 02:07:14,834
how strong you stood when
your parents were against us.

1564
02:07:15,376 --> 02:07:16,084
Everything came back to me.

1565
02:07:17,751 --> 02:07:20,542
That’s when I realized what a fool I’d been.

1566
02:07:24,001 --> 02:07:29,084
It didn't even take one full train ride
to realize that our love was real.

1567
02:07:31,709 --> 02:07:34,709
But I just couldn't find the courage to tell you the truth.

1568
02:07:35,834 --> 02:07:37,417
After everything I’d done...

1569
02:07:38,251 --> 02:07:39,917
I couldn't bear to face you.

1570
02:07:42,251 --> 02:07:45,126
Then, a few days later, I got a call from you.

1571
02:07:45,626 --> 02:07:47,501
I wanted to explain everything,

1572
02:07:47,792 --> 02:07:49,708
Nivi, please try to understand.
I'll explain everything to you.

1573
02:07:49,709 --> 02:07:51,167
Get lost Ajay.
- But you weren’t in any state to listen.

1574
02:07:51,834 --> 02:07:53,459
I tried so many times after that,

1575
02:07:54,959 --> 02:07:56,209
but you’d blocked me everywhere.

1576
02:07:57,084 --> 02:07:57,959
Hello! Nivi...

1577
02:07:58,167 --> 02:08:00,416
I didn't know what to do, so I finally called Siri.

1578
02:08:00,417 --> 02:08:01,750
Siri, please ask Nivi to unblock my number.

1579
02:08:01,751 --> 02:08:03,417
Ajay, she’s moved on.

1580
02:08:05,834 --> 02:08:07,459
She has a new roommate named Steven.

1581
02:08:07,667 --> 02:08:09,876
They're actually getting married in three days.

1582
02:08:10,167 --> 02:08:11,792
Honestly, she's been through enough.

1583
02:08:12,042 --> 02:08:14,042
Her life is finally looking up now.

1584
02:08:14,417 --> 02:08:17,209
Don't ever try to contact her or meet her again.

1585
02:08:18,292 --> 02:08:19,584
After talking to Siri, I felt...

1586
02:08:20,292 --> 02:08:22,084
at least you were happy.

1587
02:08:23,001 --> 02:08:24,209
I realised at that point...

1588
02:08:25,584 --> 02:08:26,667
I really don't deserve you, Nivi.

1589
02:08:28,542 --> 02:08:29,876
After Steven's passing,

1590
02:08:30,251 --> 02:08:32,584
I thought if I reached out then, it would look like
I was just taking advantage of the situation,

1591
02:08:32,792 --> 02:08:33,834
so I stayed away.

1592
02:08:36,042 --> 02:08:38,959
Even now, I'm only telling you
all this because you asked...

1593
02:08:39,376 --> 02:08:41,251
otherwise, you would have never known the truth.

1594
02:08:56,167 --> 02:08:57,917
I won’t ask how your meeting went.

1595
02:08:58,667 --> 02:09:00,084
And I won’t ask why you’re not asking.

1596
02:09:00,876 --> 02:09:03,417
At least tell me why you're back so soon?

1597
02:09:04,042 --> 02:09:06,751
And can I know why you showed up
after saying you wouldn't come?

1598
02:09:07,751 --> 02:09:09,751
What? Me? Are you losing it?

1599
02:09:10,709 --> 02:09:13,084
I can feel your presence when
you're around, Steven.

1600
02:09:14,126 --> 02:09:15,042
I know you were there.

1601
02:09:19,501 --> 02:09:20,667
I didn't overhear the whole thing.

1602
02:09:21,167 --> 02:09:21,959
That's another lie.

1603
02:09:22,876 --> 02:09:24,876
And what about everything he said?
Is that the truth?

1604
02:09:25,667 --> 02:09:28,334
He’s just spinning tales,
trying to manipulate you with his words.

1605
02:09:29,126 --> 02:09:30,376
If he really wanted to deceive me...

1606
02:09:31,126 --> 02:09:32,959
he would have married me without
ever mentioning Jyo.

1607
02:09:33,292 --> 02:09:33,917
So what?

1608
02:09:34,126 --> 02:09:35,876
Are you giving him a 'good guy' certificate now?

1609
02:09:36,209 --> 02:09:37,834
It's not about whether he's good or bad.

1610
02:09:38,126 --> 02:09:39,459
I'm just saying he's not a cheater.

1611
02:09:40,959 --> 02:09:42,251
Fine. I'm glad.

1612
02:09:54,792 --> 02:09:55,376
Steven...

1613
02:09:56,417 --> 02:09:56,959
Yes, tell me.

1614
02:09:58,334 --> 02:09:59,542
You’re my whole world.

1615
02:10:01,667 --> 02:10:02,667
You’re my everything.

1616
02:10:05,542 --> 02:10:06,459
It’s not Ajay...

1617
02:10:07,167 --> 02:10:12,334
out of everyone in the world,
it’s you I love the most.

1618
02:10:17,751 --> 02:10:21,375
It would’ve been better if you’d said that back there.

1619
02:10:21,376 --> 02:10:23,042
Oh, I told him there, too!

1620
02:10:24,876 --> 02:10:25,792
I made it very clear to Ajay...

1621
02:10:27,084 --> 02:10:28,584
there’s no one in my heart but Steven.

1622
02:10:29,376 --> 02:10:32,501
I told him not to hold out any hope.

1623
02:10:33,417 --> 02:10:34,001
Okay?

1624
02:10:34,834 --> 02:10:35,334
Okay.

1625
02:10:39,376 --> 02:10:40,501
Wait, clothes are getting soaked!

1626
02:10:44,792 --> 02:10:46,876
That’s fine, but what did he say to that?

1627
02:10:47,292 --> 02:10:48,709
He’s not the type to make a scene.

1628
02:10:49,251 --> 02:10:50,084
He understood.

1629
02:10:50,459 --> 02:10:51,917
But he suggested we stay friends.

1630
02:10:52,501 --> 02:10:53,417
Friends? What does that even mean?

1631
02:10:53,917 --> 02:10:55,084
Not what you’re thinking.

1632
02:10:55,209 --> 02:10:56,584
Just casual acquaintances...
the ‘hi and bye’ type.

1633
02:10:57,376 --> 02:11:00,917
Honestly, unless I get a job at his company,
I’m not even interested in seeing him again.

1634
02:11:04,001 --> 02:11:05,084
A job? At his company?

1635
02:11:05,626 --> 02:11:07,791
He mentioned there were some vacancies
and suggested I give it a try.

1636
02:11:07,792 --> 02:11:08,417
I said okay.

1637
02:11:09,167 --> 02:11:10,959
Was there really no other company
in the city where you could find work?

1638
02:11:12,167 --> 02:11:13,959
The job market is terrible right now, Steven.

1639
02:11:14,084 --> 02:11:16,334
You’ve seen how hard I’ve been
struggling these past two months.

1640
02:11:17,459 --> 02:11:18,292
When is the interview?

1641
02:11:18,834 --> 02:11:20,001
Tomorrow evening.

1642
02:11:20,459 --> 02:11:21,209
You won’t get the job.

1643
02:11:21,917 --> 02:11:22,791
Steven, please!

1644
02:11:22,792 --> 02:11:23,791
A spirit’s curse is never in vain.

1645
02:11:23,792 --> 02:11:24,709
You won't get the job.
Mark my words!

1646
02:11:26,167 --> 02:11:28,375
Congrats! You nailed the interview.

1647
02:11:28,376 --> 02:11:31,084
And a ₹25 LPA package?
That's a crazy deal!

1648
02:11:32,251 --> 02:11:33,333
Super Bro.

1649
02:11:33,334 --> 02:11:34,376
Can you refer us too?

1650
02:11:34,792 --> 02:11:37,709
We'll all join your company.
- I'll definitely try.

1651
02:11:43,334 --> 02:11:44,792
Then we can all hang out together, right?

1652
02:11:46,126 --> 02:11:48,126
I don’t know, I’m still a bit confused.

1653
02:11:48,709 --> 02:11:49,667
Isn't it obvious?

1654
02:11:49,792 --> 02:11:52,625
All those lines like "First love isn't everything"
sound great in movies.

1655
02:11:52,626 --> 02:11:54,709
But in real life...
first love is always first love.

1656
02:12:12,126 --> 02:12:13,042
Sorry, Steven.

1657
02:12:13,959 --> 02:12:18,917
I invited him because everyone
wanted to celebrate my new job.

1658
02:12:22,292 --> 02:12:23,542
Should we just head home?

1659
02:12:25,209 --> 02:12:25,876
No need.

1660
02:12:26,667 --> 02:12:27,584
You stay and enjoy.

1661
02:12:29,292 --> 02:12:31,792
Steven, please understand...

1662
02:12:33,584 --> 02:12:36,042
Nivi! What time are we leaving tomorrow?

1663
02:12:36,834 --> 02:12:37,584
3 o’clock.

1664
02:12:37,917 --> 02:12:38,667
Okay.

1665
02:12:39,917 --> 02:12:40,584
Where are you going?

1666
02:12:41,667 --> 02:12:44,167
Surya acted in an independent film.

1667
02:12:44,459 --> 02:12:46,876
The premiere is tomorrow, and he invited us.

1668
02:12:50,876 --> 02:12:51,876
We’re going, right?

1669
02:12:52,584 --> 02:12:53,959
I'm not coming.
You guys go ahead.

1670
02:13:00,917 --> 02:13:03,417
Could you at least change that expression
on your face? I can't stand to look at it.

1671
02:13:03,751 --> 02:13:05,417
Then you should've brought
someone you actually like.

1672
02:13:09,084 --> 02:13:12,751
Nivi! Why are you sitting all alone?
Come join us!

1673
02:13:13,459 --> 02:13:14,459
I'm good... it's okay.

1674
02:13:17,834 --> 02:13:21,084
I'm telling you now...
if the movie gets boring, I'm walking out halfway.

1675
02:13:22,292 --> 02:13:23,459
Fine. Just watch the movie first.

1676
02:13:42,792 --> 02:13:44,334
I heard he's a really good writer.

1677
02:13:44,584 --> 02:13:47,251
His stories are never boring.

1678
02:13:52,584 --> 02:13:53,876
This is your story, Steven.

1679
02:13:54,209 --> 02:13:56,917
The film is finished and ready for release.

1680
02:13:57,584 --> 02:14:02,001
The producer is screening it for his
close circle, and we were invited too.

1681
02:14:13,084 --> 02:14:14,626
I'll go sit with our friends.

1682
02:14:15,876 --> 02:14:16,959
You just enjoy this moment.

1683
02:15:39,126 --> 02:15:41,125
Congratulations!
Nice movie.

1684
02:15:41,126 --> 02:15:41,792
Thank you sir.

1685
02:15:51,001 --> 02:15:51,792
Thank you.

1686
02:15:58,959 --> 02:16:00,084
The movie was wonderful, sir.

1687
02:16:00,251 --> 02:16:01,708
Congratulations!
It was superb!

1688
02:16:01,709 --> 02:16:02,167
Thank you.

1689
02:16:02,334 --> 02:16:03,416
It was superb!
- Thank you.

1690
02:16:03,417 --> 02:16:04,791
They all are my friends.
- Thank you.

1691
02:16:04,792 --> 02:16:06,292
I'm Chaitanya, sir...
Steven's friend.

1692
02:16:10,751 --> 02:16:13,417
I didn't pay anything to Steven.

1693
02:16:15,001 --> 02:16:21,626
I don't know what his dreams were or how
he would have used this money if he were still with us.

1694
02:16:22,251 --> 02:16:25,542
But if you know what he wanted,
take this and see that those things are done.

1695
02:16:25,667 --> 02:16:26,792
It would make him truly happy.

1696
02:16:31,334 --> 02:16:32,167
Take it, dear.

1697
02:16:32,584 --> 02:16:33,417
This is his money.

1698
02:16:44,126 --> 02:16:45,001
Well, Mr. Writer?

1699
02:16:45,334 --> 02:16:46,833
You seem really happy.

1700
02:16:46,834 --> 02:16:47,917
I'm really happy.

1701
02:16:48,792 --> 02:16:51,459
So... what are you going to
do with all this money?

1702
02:16:59,167 --> 02:17:00,459
Just a minute...
- Okay.

1703
02:17:02,917 --> 02:17:04,292
How did you even know about this?

1704
02:17:04,751 --> 02:17:05,834
I saw it a long time ago.

1705
02:17:06,376 --> 02:17:07,709
But at the time, I didn't have the money.

1706
02:17:12,584 --> 02:17:14,126
It’s beautiful, isn’t it?
- Very beautiful.

1707
02:17:15,542 --> 02:17:18,042
It's so expensive, though, Steven.

1708
02:17:18,959 --> 02:17:21,417
It only has value because you're wearing it.

1709
02:17:23,501 --> 02:17:24,501
Shall I pack it up for you, Madam?

1710
02:17:26,834 --> 02:17:27,501
Yes, please.

1711
02:17:33,084 --> 02:17:35,334
So, what are you going to do
with the rest of the money?

1712
02:17:40,209 --> 02:17:41,626
Vignesh! Come here.

1713
02:17:42,501 --> 02:17:43,209
Just a minute...

1714
02:17:49,167 --> 02:17:52,167
Remember I told you about that man
who used to come by and ask about you?

1715
02:17:52,334 --> 02:17:55,041
He wrote a movie story and got paid for it.

1716
02:17:55,042 --> 02:17:56,792
He asked me to give this to you.
Go on... take it.

1717
02:17:57,917 --> 02:17:58,626
Take it, son.

1718
02:18:07,792 --> 02:18:12,084
He recently got a job in the RRB
and starts in two months.

1719
02:18:12,334 --> 02:18:16,667
I was so worried about how he’d manage,
but this is all a blessing from God.

1720
02:18:18,126 --> 02:18:20,209
Oh, I forgot..have something to eat, dear!

1721
02:18:20,376 --> 02:18:20,917
No, thank you, sir.

1722
02:18:21,626 --> 02:18:23,959
Come here for a second, Brother.

1723
02:18:24,126 --> 02:18:24,667
I'm coming.

1724
02:18:24,917 --> 02:18:25,584
Wait dear.

1725
02:18:27,126 --> 02:18:29,626
Hey, can't you see I'm talking to that girl?
What's your problem?

1726
02:18:33,917 --> 02:18:35,334
Steven, what happened?

1727
02:18:38,667 --> 02:18:39,501
Find out what’s going on with him.

1728
02:18:40,584 --> 02:18:41,209
What?

1729
02:18:41,376 --> 02:18:43,084
Find out why he’s stopped talking to his father.

1730
02:18:47,001 --> 02:18:47,792
Brother!

1731
02:18:48,792 --> 02:18:49,376
Tell me, dear.

1732
02:18:49,667 --> 02:18:54,501
Steven always used to tell me that Vignesh
would talk to his late father.

1733
02:18:55,167 --> 02:18:56,001
But now...

1734
02:18:56,209 --> 02:18:58,709
His father has stopped appearing to him now, dear.

1735
02:19:05,167 --> 02:19:08,001
It was his father’s deepest wish
that he land a government job.

1736
02:19:12,084 --> 02:19:14,875
Until that happened, his father’s spirit
would wake him up every single morning,

1737
02:19:14,876 --> 02:19:16,459
stay by his side while he studied,
and keep pushing him forward.

1738
02:19:17,876 --> 02:19:20,626
Once he finally got the job, he stopped appearing.

1739
02:19:28,501 --> 02:19:31,459
They say that once their earthly desires
are fulfilled, souls finally move on to the next world.

1740
02:19:32,126 --> 02:19:33,334
I suppose we have to believe that’s the truth, dear.

1741
02:19:48,876 --> 02:19:52,459
Just like Selva said, I’m going to
have to leave you too.

1742
02:19:53,376 --> 02:19:54,709
I used to wonder what my wishes were...

1743
02:19:55,542 --> 02:19:57,376
I thought I had no value in this world.

1744
02:19:58,376 --> 02:20:00,376
But Murugan’s mom treats me like a god.

1745
02:20:01,084 --> 02:20:03,542
I wanted to see my name on the big screen just once.

1746
02:20:05,001 --> 02:20:07,542
If all those dreams have come true and I’m still here…

1747
02:20:09,584 --> 02:20:11,376
what could that one unfulfilled wish be?

1748
02:20:14,917 --> 02:20:16,417
Shall I tell you what it is, Steven?

1749
02:20:18,292 --> 02:20:20,834
As long as I’m alive,
you just want to stay with me.

1750
02:20:25,709 --> 02:20:26,417
You’re right.

1751
02:20:27,126 --> 02:20:29,959
What bigger wish could I have than being with you?

1752
02:20:31,417 --> 02:20:33,667
I’ll be with you forever, no matter what happens.

1753
02:20:34,251 --> 02:20:34,751
Yes.

1754
02:20:35,417 --> 02:20:36,001
Deal?

1755
02:20:36,584 --> 02:20:37,167
Deal.

1756
02:20:39,084 --> 02:20:40,542
I think your food is here, go grab it.

1757
02:20:50,334 --> 02:20:51,084
Where’s the food?

1758
02:20:55,917 --> 02:20:56,584
Hello, Madam?

1759
02:20:57,876 --> 02:20:58,667
What happened?

1760
02:20:59,709 --> 02:21:00,667
Ajay’s here.

1761
02:21:06,917 --> 02:21:07,542
Hi!

1762
02:21:07,959 --> 02:21:08,376
Hi!

1763
02:21:13,917 --> 02:21:18,750
You haven’t picked up my calls for two days,
so I just wanted to check on you.

1764
02:21:18,751 --> 02:21:19,251
That's it.

1765
02:21:19,917 --> 02:21:20,501
He saw you right?

1766
02:21:20,792 --> 02:21:22,250
Ask him to leave... tell him to leave.

1767
02:21:22,251 --> 02:21:22,834
May I come in?

1768
02:21:24,834 --> 02:21:25,417
May I come in?

1769
02:21:31,292 --> 02:21:31,792
Nivi?

1770
02:21:33,334 --> 02:21:34,084
May I come in?

1771
02:21:34,959 --> 02:21:35,834
Yeah, please.

1772
02:21:45,917 --> 02:21:47,250
Damn, it’s raining.

1773
02:21:47,251 --> 02:21:48,917
It just had to start raining
at exactly the wrong time, didn’t it?

1774
02:21:50,292 --> 02:21:51,667
This is such nice weather, isn’t it?

1775
02:21:56,042 --> 02:21:57,584
Nivi, are you okay?

1776
02:21:59,042 --> 02:22:00,251
Yeah, I’m okay.

1777
02:22:01,667 --> 02:22:02,626
I know it’s hard.

1778
02:22:03,167 --> 02:22:06,042
Nivi, but at some point,
you’ve got to move on from Steven.

1779
02:22:07,792 --> 02:22:09,542
We all have to move on eventually.

1780
02:22:10,417 --> 02:22:12,626
Besides, people who pass away
never come back, do they?

1781
02:22:13,334 --> 02:22:14,416
I’m right here, you idiot!

1782
02:22:14,417 --> 02:22:15,542
You’re just the only one who can’t see me.

1783
02:22:18,709 --> 02:22:20,334
So, have you talked to your mother recently?

1784
02:22:20,792 --> 02:22:22,334
About what?

1785
02:22:23,126 --> 02:22:26,417
Well, my uncle met her at a function recently and...

1786
02:22:26,876 --> 02:22:27,501
And?

1787
02:22:28,001 --> 02:22:30,834
He mentioned our patch-up,
and she was really happy to hear it.

1788
02:22:33,417 --> 02:22:34,042
A patch-up?

1789
02:22:35,042 --> 02:22:35,667
What patch-up?!

1790
02:22:35,959 --> 02:22:37,709
No, no... I meant just as friends.

1791
02:22:39,834 --> 02:22:40,417
Oh... friends.

1792
02:22:44,417 --> 02:22:44,834
What else?

1793
02:22:46,792 --> 02:22:47,292
Tell me.

1794
02:22:49,001 --> 02:22:49,626
You should say...

1795
02:22:51,334 --> 02:22:51,959
You should say...

1796
02:22:52,334 --> 02:22:54,416
What else could there be to talk about?
Bring that speaker and put on some music!

1797
02:22:54,417 --> 02:22:55,458
He just needs to be quiet for a minute.

1798
02:22:55,459 --> 02:22:57,459
My nerves are shot just wondering
what lies he’s going to tell next!

1799
02:22:58,417 --> 02:22:59,667
Ajay, just one second...

1800
02:23:05,584 --> 02:23:10,167
"What is this magic, my dear?
Has a sweet trance taken over?"

1801
02:23:11,876 --> 02:23:12,292
Wow!

1802
02:23:12,667 --> 02:23:13,251
Nivi...

1803
02:23:13,917 --> 02:23:15,459
You still remember my favorite song?

1804
02:23:15,876 --> 02:23:20,251
"What is this magic, my dear?
Has a sweet trance taken over?"

1805
02:23:21,042 --> 02:23:22,291
"Has Indra's heavenly realm united you and me?"

1806
02:23:22,292 --> 02:23:23,459
I swear, I didn't know.

1807
02:23:23,584 --> 02:23:25,292
"Has Indra's heavenly realm united you and me?"

1808
02:23:28,709 --> 02:23:29,292
Thanks.

1809
02:23:30,709 --> 02:23:32,001
I actually had a lovely time.

1810
02:23:33,167 --> 02:23:34,501
Okay, okay, that’s enough.
Tell him to get going now!

1811
02:23:37,167 --> 02:23:38,875
I've got a headache.

1812
02:23:38,876 --> 02:23:40,333
Yeah, sure, you should go ahead and get some rest.

1813
02:23:40,334 --> 02:23:41,376
I’ll leave as soon as the cab gets here.

1814
02:23:41,709 --> 02:23:42,084
Okay?

1815
02:23:44,042 --> 02:23:45,376
This is so stressful!

1816
02:23:47,042 --> 02:23:48,417
His cab isn't booking.

1817
02:23:52,084 --> 02:23:53,501
It's a rainy night...

1818
02:23:54,042 --> 02:23:55,042
she's in the bedroom,

1819
02:23:55,417 --> 02:23:58,084
he's in the hall, and here I am,
completely powerless.

1820
02:24:01,292 --> 02:24:03,376
This is what true spiritual torment feels like, isn't it?

1821
02:24:04,084 --> 02:24:07,292
Why did I even come back when she called?

1822
02:24:07,584 --> 02:24:09,292
Just to see all this?

1823
02:24:54,626 --> 02:24:56,084
He's not as big an idiot as we thought.

1824
02:25:01,167 --> 02:25:02,626
Still hasn’t gotten his cab...

1825
02:25:04,459 --> 02:25:06,042
What is he staring at?

1826
02:25:32,167 --> 02:25:34,126
Hello?
Yes, I'm coming now.

1827
02:25:48,959 --> 02:25:49,876
Yes, Dad.

1828
02:25:50,417 --> 02:25:53,417
Nivi, can you come to the village immediately?

1829
02:25:53,667 --> 02:25:54,959
Why, Dad? What happened?

1830
02:25:55,667 --> 02:25:58,959
Your mother suddenly had severe chest pain...
we’ve brought her to the hospital.

1831
02:25:59,209 --> 02:26:00,250
The doctor just finished checking her.

1832
02:26:00,251 --> 02:26:01,834
What happened? How is she now?

1833
02:26:02,251 --> 02:26:03,834
It’s quite serious, Nivi.

1834
02:26:04,084 --> 02:26:06,084
They’re saying she needs an urgent operation.

1835
02:26:06,709 --> 02:26:08,126
She really wants to see you.

1836
02:26:08,792 --> 02:26:10,917
Please, start for the village right away.

1837
02:26:11,834 --> 02:26:13,001
I'm coming immediately, Dad.

1838
02:26:16,459 --> 02:26:17,584
Steven, what are you doing here?

1839
02:26:18,084 --> 02:26:19,501
I just got a call that Mom is very unwell.

1840
02:26:19,751 --> 02:26:20,834
We have to go to the village right now!

1841
02:26:22,084 --> 02:26:23,084
Why are you looking at me like that?
Let’s go!

1842
02:26:30,167 --> 02:26:30,709
Auto!

1843
02:26:32,542 --> 02:26:33,126
Damn!

1844
02:26:34,917 --> 02:26:37,542
I can't get a cab.
We're going to be late for the train.

1845
02:26:39,917 --> 02:26:41,042
What's wrong with you?
Why are you like this?

1846
02:26:42,876 --> 02:26:43,876
Say something!

1847
02:26:44,501 --> 02:26:45,667
Why did you lie to me?

1848
02:26:47,417 --> 02:26:48,001
What?

1849
02:26:49,126 --> 02:26:51,167
Why did you hide the fact
that you kissed Ajay?

1850
02:26:59,167 --> 02:26:59,917
Steven...

1851
02:27:00,792 --> 02:27:02,501
can we please talk about this later?

1852
02:27:03,584 --> 02:27:05,166
No, not later. You need to tell me right now.

1853
02:27:05,167 --> 02:27:06,959
Look, I’m dealing with a lot of stress right now.
Don’t start creating drama!

1854
02:27:09,126 --> 02:27:09,876
Drama?

1855
02:27:11,001 --> 02:27:11,834
Yes, that's exactly what it is!

1856
02:27:12,751 --> 02:27:15,709
When I say we’ll talk later,
just listen and try to understand!

1857
02:27:18,459 --> 02:27:19,542
Madam, where do you want to go?

1858
02:27:20,751 --> 02:27:22,083
Brother, I need to go to Central Station.

1859
02:27:22,084 --> 02:27:23,084
Get in, I’ll take you there.

1860
02:27:29,626 --> 02:27:31,917
Okay Dad, I’ll call you once I’m on the train.

1861
02:27:32,126 --> 02:27:32,792
Take care.

1862
02:27:36,959 --> 02:27:38,709
You still haven’t answered my question.

1863
02:27:39,584 --> 02:27:40,667
Have you lost your mind, Steven?

1864
02:27:48,626 --> 02:27:49,751
Just be quiet for a minute.

1865
02:27:51,917 --> 02:27:53,334
Answer me. Why did you lie to me?

1866
02:27:54,459 --> 02:27:57,584
Because I knew you wouldn’t have the 'broad-minded'
perspective to understand if I told you.

1867
02:28:06,251 --> 02:28:08,084
And did your 'broad mindset' stop with that kiss,

1868
02:28:09,251 --> 02:28:10,542
or was there more to it?

1869
02:28:14,626 --> 02:28:15,209
Steven...

1870
02:28:15,876 --> 02:28:17,125
please don't embarrass me like this.

1871
02:28:17,126 --> 02:28:19,251
Just tell me... did it happen or not?

1872
02:28:21,792 --> 02:28:22,376
It didn't!

1873
02:28:22,584 --> 02:28:24,042
How can I make you believe me?

1874
02:28:25,417 --> 02:28:26,459
Look into my eyes and tell me.

1875
02:28:29,084 --> 02:28:30,167
it didn't happen, okay?

1876
02:28:33,126 --> 02:28:34,542
There’s no need to make such a big deal out of it.

1877
02:28:34,959 --> 02:28:37,167
It was just a kiss, and we
were in a relationship back then.

1878
02:28:37,917 --> 02:28:40,042
Well, we were in a 'relationship' for
ten days before the wedding too...

1879
02:28:40,459 --> 02:28:41,709
so why didn't you ever kiss me?

1880
02:28:46,209 --> 02:28:47,334
I'm asking you. Tell me.

1881
02:28:47,917 --> 02:28:49,126
The moment just never came, that’s all.

1882
02:28:51,834 --> 02:28:52,792
And it’ll never come now, will it?

1883
02:28:54,709 --> 02:28:55,251
What?

1884
02:28:55,501 --> 02:28:56,792
Is that why you joined his company?

1885
02:28:58,542 --> 02:28:59,876
I remember everything you said to me.

1886
02:29:00,167 --> 02:29:05,417
You said you wanted to touch me,
to hug me, to kiss me...

1887
02:29:05,542 --> 02:29:07,417
Since I can't do any of that,
you've grown closer to him, haven't you?

1888
02:29:08,167 --> 02:29:10,167
Steven, stop talking such nonsense!

1889
02:29:10,292 --> 02:29:11,917
Is love only about those physical things?

1890
02:29:12,042 --> 02:29:13,666
Is there no love without them?

1891
02:29:13,667 --> 02:29:15,001
Steven, please, stop this.

1892
02:29:15,751 --> 02:29:19,084
Aside from that three-letter word,
is there anything I haven't done for you?

1893
02:29:19,376 --> 02:29:21,083
Steven, stop this right now!

1894
02:29:21,084 --> 02:29:23,458
Tell me! Did I not take care of you properly?
Tell me!

1895
02:29:23,459 --> 02:29:24,542
Steven, stop this!

1896
02:29:29,001 --> 02:29:29,751
What's wrong, brother?

1897
02:29:35,709 --> 02:29:36,667
Any problem?

1898
02:29:42,292 --> 02:29:44,001
Why did you stop here?
We have to get to the station.

1899
02:29:57,292 --> 02:29:59,376
Ramesh! What brings you here at this hour?

1900
02:30:00,251 --> 02:30:02,667
I brought you some fresh merchandise, bro.

1901
02:30:02,876 --> 02:30:03,792
How do you like it?

1902
02:30:04,667 --> 02:30:05,917
Very nice.

1903
02:30:06,376 --> 02:30:07,584
I want her first.

1904
02:30:07,792 --> 02:30:08,876
First, go from here.

1905
02:30:09,959 --> 02:30:11,042
I'm talking to you.
Get out of here!

1906
02:30:17,417 --> 02:30:18,709
Hey, run!
Catch her!

1907
02:30:21,209 --> 02:30:21,792
Where is she?

1908
02:30:22,417 --> 02:30:22,792
Come.

1909
02:30:23,709 --> 02:30:25,542
Hey, where is she?
Come on...

1910
02:30:40,542 --> 02:30:40,959
Come...

1911
02:30:43,126 --> 02:30:43,584
Go.

1912
02:30:44,417 --> 02:30:44,792
This way.

1913
02:30:55,167 --> 02:30:55,584
Come...

1914
02:31:06,042 --> 02:31:06,667
Nivi!

1915
02:31:10,501 --> 02:31:11,042
Nivi!

1916
02:31:16,792 --> 02:31:17,459
Nivi!

1917
02:31:27,459 --> 02:31:28,501
Hey!

1918
02:31:32,834 --> 02:31:34,126
Hey!

1919
02:31:37,542 --> 02:31:39,542
Hey, where did you go?

1920
02:31:44,334 --> 02:31:45,042
Help!

1921
02:31:45,667 --> 02:31:46,959
Help! Help!

1922
02:31:48,042 --> 02:31:48,751
Help!

1923
02:31:49,042 --> 02:31:51,126
Wait. I'll call you once I'm done with her.

1924
02:31:53,167 --> 02:31:54,126
Hurry up!

1925
02:31:54,376 --> 02:31:56,501
Brother! Brother! Please help, brother!

1926
02:31:57,917 --> 02:31:59,292
Hey! Where are you running to?

1927
02:32:35,834 --> 02:32:37,001
I’ll go next.

1928
02:32:37,584 --> 02:32:38,792
Go, go!

1929
02:33:15,959 --> 02:33:17,417
Hey, what happened?

1930
02:35:37,917 --> 02:35:39,417
You’ll be alright; please don’t be afraid.

1931
02:35:39,626 --> 02:35:40,251
No one else is coming

1932
02:35:41,876 --> 02:35:42,792
Let’s get out of here first...

1933
02:35:44,376 --> 02:35:45,167
I'm talking to you.

1934
02:35:45,292 --> 02:35:46,376
We'll miss the train.
Let's get out of here first.

1935
02:35:48,792 --> 02:35:49,459
Where is your scarf?

1936
02:35:50,042 --> 02:35:50,667
Where is your scarf?

1937
02:35:53,876 --> 02:35:54,500
Nothing is going to happen to you.

1938
02:35:54,501 --> 02:35:55,501
As long as I’m here, you’re safe.

1939
02:35:55,667 --> 02:35:56,501
As long as Steven is with you...

1940
02:36:20,251 --> 02:36:21,084
Nothing is going to happen to you.

1941
02:36:22,251 --> 02:36:22,876
I’m here for you.

1942
02:36:32,001 --> 02:36:32,709
Nothing will happen to you.

1943
02:36:34,042 --> 02:36:35,042
I won't let anything happen to you.

1944
02:36:50,917 --> 02:36:51,626
Nothing will happen to you.

1945
02:36:52,417 --> 02:36:53,042
I’m here for you.

1946
02:37:10,501 --> 02:37:12,126
Nivi, are you… are you okay?

1947
02:37:14,667 --> 02:37:15,334
Sorry Nivi.

1948
02:37:15,876 --> 02:37:18,834
I started as soon as I saw your message,
but I got late.

1949
02:37:20,251 --> 02:37:21,959
It’s okay now. I’m here, right?

1950
02:37:22,084 --> 02:37:23,501
I’ll take care of everything. Okay?

1951
02:37:30,917 --> 02:37:32,167
Why did you leave all alone?

1952
02:37:32,501 --> 02:37:33,876
If you had told me, I would have come with you.

1953
02:38:52,917 --> 02:38:53,376
Hello...

1954
02:38:54,167 --> 02:38:55,917
It's okay, man. She's fine.

1955
02:38:56,459 --> 02:38:58,376
I think she's just in shock.

1956
02:39:00,417 --> 02:39:00,834
Hey!

1957
02:39:01,292 --> 02:39:04,209
If I bring up my feelings at a time like this,
it'll look like I'm taking advantage of the situation.

1958
02:39:05,167 --> 02:39:05,959
That's not right.

1959
02:39:08,209 --> 02:39:09,751
First, let her get through this.

1960
02:39:11,292 --> 02:39:12,167
Hang on. I'll call you back.

1961
02:39:24,667 --> 02:39:25,876
Nivi, this way...

1962
02:39:28,001 --> 02:39:29,166
Uncle...
- Nivi...

1963
02:39:29,167 --> 02:39:30,626
Hi, Doctor.
- Have all the reports come in?

1964
02:39:30,917 --> 02:39:31,709
Yes, we have all the reports.

1965
02:39:32,042 --> 02:39:34,167
We can operate once the
blood pressure is under control.

1966
02:39:45,751 --> 02:39:46,584
Nivi!

1967
02:39:48,126 --> 02:39:52,584
I wasn’t sure if you’d make it here before the surgery.

1968
02:39:55,584 --> 02:39:57,292
I don’t know if I’ll ever have the
chance to ask you again...

1969
02:39:58,334 --> 02:40:00,001
will you give me your word, Nivi?

1970
02:40:01,292 --> 02:40:01,959
Tell me, Mom.

1971
02:40:03,417 --> 02:40:05,251
Promise me you'll get married.

1972
02:40:08,459 --> 02:40:10,459
Just give me your word, Nivi.

1973
02:40:11,167 --> 02:40:15,042
Then I'll go into the operation without a worry.

1974
02:40:16,917 --> 02:40:19,251
Kala... why bring this up now?

1975
02:40:20,459 --> 02:40:25,251
I'll agree to the operation only if Nivi agrees to get married.

1976
02:40:26,001 --> 02:40:27,834
Mom... that's not it...
– Just tell her you'll get married.

1977
02:40:32,542 --> 02:40:33,709
Just tell her you'll get married.

1978
02:40:40,542 --> 02:40:42,334
Nothing is more important than saving a life.

1979
02:40:42,959 --> 02:40:44,126
Please... tell her you'll get married.

1980
02:40:51,209 --> 02:40:52,334
I'll get married, Mom.

1981
02:40:59,167 --> 02:41:00,917
You won't break your promise, will you, Nivi?

1982
02:41:03,751 --> 02:41:05,209
Tell her that I'll marry Ajay.

1983
02:41:16,751 --> 02:41:17,584
Please tell her.

1984
02:41:18,417 --> 02:41:19,876
It's time for the operation.
Tell her quickly.

1985
02:41:29,917 --> 02:41:30,709
I mean it, Mom.

1986
02:41:32,001 --> 02:41:32,542
And not just anyone...

1987
02:41:33,917 --> 02:41:35,001
I’ll marry Ajay.

1988
02:41:40,126 --> 02:41:40,876
Ajay!

1989
02:41:42,001 --> 02:41:44,459
is what Nivi said true?

1990
02:41:46,626 --> 02:41:48,251
Yes, Auntie. It's true.
I'll marry her.

1991
02:42:44,126 --> 02:42:45,751
Why did you make me say that, Steven?

1992
02:42:49,001 --> 02:42:49,834
I'm asking you.

1993
02:42:50,834 --> 02:42:52,709
Because that's what was bound
to happen sooner or later.

1994
02:42:54,417 --> 02:42:54,917
Go...

1995
02:42:56,334 --> 02:42:57,542
Live your life.

1996
02:43:05,126 --> 02:43:06,209
Is it really you saying this?

1997
02:43:07,709 --> 02:43:08,417
Tell me the truth.

1998
02:43:10,876 --> 02:43:11,959
Look into my eyes and tell me!

1999
02:43:14,751 --> 02:43:15,709
I am telling you the truth.

2000
02:43:18,876 --> 02:43:19,459
Just go.

2001
02:43:30,209 --> 02:43:31,417
You are my life, Steven…

2002
02:43:34,501 --> 02:43:37,792
I can’t live without you.

2003
02:43:40,459 --> 02:43:44,042
Just thinking about it makes my head spin.

2004
02:43:45,167 --> 02:43:48,958
It feels like someone's choking me, Steven.

2005
02:43:48,959 --> 02:43:49,792
It's not someone else...

2006
02:43:50,376 --> 02:43:50,834
it's me.

2007
02:43:54,001 --> 02:43:55,459
I'm the reason you can't breathe.

2008
02:43:56,459 --> 02:43:59,792
The farther you stay from me,
the more peace you'll find.

2009
02:44:01,876 --> 02:44:03,251
Maybe not today... maybe in a few days...

2010
02:44:03,667 --> 02:44:05,084
Or even a few years from now...

2011
02:44:05,459 --> 02:44:08,376
But staying away from me is the right thing to do.
- Don’t talk like that, Steven...

2012
02:44:08,917 --> 02:44:10,791
I'll beg you...

2013
02:44:10,792 --> 02:44:11,459
please…

2014
02:44:13,876 --> 02:44:15,292
I'll beg you...

2015
02:44:26,167 --> 02:44:28,167
I just want you to stay with me
for the rest of my life, Steven.

2016
02:44:29,292 --> 02:44:30,542
I don’t need anything else.

2017
02:44:33,042 --> 02:44:34,626
I used to think the same thing...

2018
02:44:35,917 --> 02:44:37,584
that being with you forever was all I wanted.

2019
02:44:40,251 --> 02:44:44,417
I thought God sent me back, saying,
'There's a girl down there who's suffering.

2020
02:44:44,709 --> 02:44:47,917
If you're not there, who will take care of her?

2021
02:44:49,709 --> 02:44:54,334
But what can I really do for you now?
I have no life, What can I do?

2022
02:44:55,209 --> 02:44:56,209
I don’t care, Steven!

2023
02:44:56,917 --> 02:44:58,084
I’ll look after myself.

2024
02:44:58,876 --> 02:45:00,083
I just need you to be with me, that’s all.

2025
02:45:00,084 --> 02:45:00,667
No.

2026
02:45:02,667 --> 02:45:04,084
Listen to me and marry Ajay.

2027
02:45:05,667 --> 02:45:07,709
He’ll take care of you much better than I ever could.

2028
02:45:08,709 --> 02:45:11,709
Steven, how can I make you understand?

2029
02:45:13,876 --> 02:45:18,084
There's no one else in my heart but you, Steven.

2030
02:45:18,334 --> 02:45:20,917
That’s only because I happened to enter your life.

2031
02:45:23,251 --> 02:45:25,792
Just once, try to imagine this story without me in it.

2032
02:45:26,459 --> 02:45:28,542
Suppose you never even knew
a guy named Steven Shankar.

2033
02:45:29,542 --> 02:45:32,959
What would you have done when Ajay
realized his mistake and came back to him?

2034
02:45:34,876 --> 02:45:36,042
This is your story.

2035
02:45:36,584 --> 02:45:37,709
I'm the one who came between you two.

2036
02:45:40,376 --> 02:45:44,126
I’m just a side character who stumbled into it.

2037
02:45:45,084 --> 02:45:46,751
You and Ajay... you are the real
hero and heroine of this tale.

2038
02:45:54,251 --> 02:45:54,792
Nivi!

2039
02:45:57,917 --> 02:45:59,292
What are you doing here all alone?

2040
02:46:01,126 --> 02:46:03,250
It’s nothing, Ajay.
I’ll be back in a minute.

2041
02:46:03,251 --> 02:46:03,959
You go ahead.

2042
02:46:05,542 --> 02:46:06,959
You only said you’d marry me
for your mom’s sake, didn’t you?

2043
02:46:09,709 --> 02:46:11,834
I know you still haven't forgotten Steven, Nivi.

2044
02:46:14,584 --> 02:46:16,751
Once the surgery is over,
I’ll talk to your mom myself.

2045
02:46:18,126 --> 02:46:21,542
You don’t need to worry about this...
the wedding isn't going to happen.

2046
02:46:23,084 --> 02:46:25,458
Ajay, that’s not true!
She really does love you, Ajay!

2047
02:46:25,459 --> 02:46:26,542
She’s going to marry you!

2048
02:46:27,917 --> 02:46:30,751
Tell him, please!
Tell him how much you care about him!"

2049
02:46:34,501 --> 02:46:35,376
Ajay is leaving...

2050
02:46:35,792 --> 02:46:37,292
Ajay is leaving...
Please, please say something!

2051
02:46:37,584 --> 02:46:41,334
If you love me even a little, call him back!

2052
02:46:45,001 --> 02:46:45,751
Please call him.

2053
02:46:45,959 --> 02:46:46,459
Ajay!

2054
02:46:51,417 --> 02:46:52,167
Come on, I’ll tell you what to say.

2055
02:46:54,667 --> 02:46:58,042
Don't ask me why... just say exactly what I tell you.

2056
02:47:05,376 --> 02:47:06,626
Ajay, you are my world.

2057
02:47:11,167 --> 02:47:12,001
Say it, please.

2058
02:47:14,376 --> 02:47:14,959
Ajay...

2059
02:47:16,126 --> 02:47:17,167
you are my world.

2060
02:47:20,917 --> 02:47:22,167
Ajay, you are my life.

2061
02:47:24,667 --> 02:47:25,584
You are my life.

2062
02:47:28,876 --> 02:47:30,167
Even more than Steven…

2063
02:47:31,167 --> 02:47:36,667
I love you… very, very… very much.

2064
02:47:46,501 --> 02:47:48,042
Uh-uh… you have to say it.

2065
02:47:50,792 --> 02:47:51,917
Even more than Steven…

2066
02:47:53,876 --> 02:47:59,501
I love you very, very, very much.

2067
02:48:30,459 --> 02:48:32,584
It's time for Steven to leave this world.

2068
02:48:37,167 --> 02:48:39,667
Now I finally understand what my true wish was.

2069
02:48:43,959 --> 02:48:45,584
It wasn't seeing my name on the silver screen...

2070
02:48:46,209 --> 02:48:48,084
Or being worshipped like a god...

2071
02:48:48,667 --> 02:48:50,834
Or spending my whole life with you.

2072
02:48:52,626 --> 02:48:56,959
My only wish is for you to live happily...
even in a world without me.

2073
02:48:59,917 --> 02:49:01,167
And only Ajay can make that happen.

2074
02:49:04,626 --> 02:49:08,792
True love isn't just about cherishing the
one you love while you're with them...

2075
02:49:09,542 --> 02:49:13,751
It's about making sure they never have to face
a life of emptiness, even after you're gone.

2076
02:49:16,459 --> 02:49:19,792
Before I go… can I hold you one last time?

2077
02:49:23,751 --> 02:49:24,792
Call Ajay.

2078
02:49:28,626 --> 02:49:29,709
Just once, please.

2079
02:49:33,417 --> 02:49:34,084
Ajay!

2080
02:50:25,209 --> 02:50:26,501
I love you so much, Nivi

2081
02:50:26,876 --> 02:50:28,251
I won't leave you ever again,
until my very last breath.

2082
02:50:43,501 --> 02:50:53,126
"Within your smile, I'll live forever,
An eternal part of who you are."

2083
02:50:53,584 --> 02:51:03,751
"In your moments of joy,
I'll always find my peace."

2084
02:51:04,167 --> 02:51:12,626
"This isn't goodbye, my friend...
I'll forever dwell within your heart."

2085
02:51:14,167 --> 02:51:22,626
"Don't think of this as farewell...
I've simply become one with you."

2086
02:51:23,459 --> 02:51:32,834
"Within your smile, I'll live forever,
An eternal part of who you are."

2087
02:51:33,501 --> 02:51:36,042
From today, you are my goddess...

2088
02:51:36,626 --> 02:51:38,083
and I am your slave.

2089
02:51:38,084 --> 02:51:43,084
"In your moments of joy,
I'll always find my peace."

2090
02:51:44,084 --> 02:51:46,626
"This isn't goodbye, my friend...
I'll forever dwell within your heart."

2091
02:51:46,751 --> 02:51:48,751
Hello, I'm Steven Shankar.

2092
02:51:49,334 --> 02:51:52,292
Once you meet me, you'll never forget me.

2093
02:51:53,834 --> 02:52:02,292
"Don't think of this as farewell...
I've simply become one with you."

2094
02:52:19,959 --> 02:52:20,626
Yes, Mom...

2095
02:52:21,417 --> 02:52:23,417
yeah, we’re leaving this evening.

2096
02:52:24,042 --> 02:52:25,334
The train is at 5:30.

2097
02:52:28,376 --> 02:52:29,209
Yes, all of us.

2098
02:52:31,876 --> 02:52:32,792
I’ll let you know.

2099
02:52:36,084 --> 02:52:37,958
Yeah, Mom, we're done shopping.

2100
02:52:37,959 --> 02:52:39,875
We bought everything, so don't worry.

2101
02:52:39,876 --> 02:52:40,834
Okay?

2102
02:52:41,126 --> 02:52:41,751
Bye.
- Madam!

2103
02:52:42,667 --> 02:52:44,167
Thank you...
- Thank you, Madam!

2104
02:52:47,251 --> 02:52:49,001
Brother! I've got off. I'm on my way.

2105
02:52:49,167 --> 02:52:52,417
I saw an aquarium shop on the way and
thought I’d stop to buy a fish. I’ll be right there.

2106
02:52:58,001 --> 02:52:59,209
Brother... can I have that fish?

2107
02:52:59,626 --> 02:53:02,084
Bro, it’s hard for a fish to live all by itself

2108
02:53:02,834 --> 02:53:04,500
I'm all alone too... don't I survive?

2109
02:53:04,501 --> 02:53:05,334
Come on, give it to me, bro.

2110
02:53:15,376 --> 02:53:20,166
"The first light of dawn is my gentle greeting,"

2111
02:53:20,167 --> 02:53:23,709
"The moonlight sings you to sleep."

2112
02:53:25,376 --> 02:53:30,209
"The whisper of the wind is my calling,"

2113
02:53:30,376 --> 02:53:34,209
"The dancing leaves are my embrace"

2114
02:53:35,417 --> 02:53:43,459
"Between every beat of your heart,
I'll always be there."

2115
02:53:45,292 --> 02:53:53,001
"Your every breath becomes my own,
As I breathe through you."

2116
02:53:55,084 --> 02:54:03,542
"This isn't goodbye, my friend...
I'll forever dwell within your heart."

2117
02:54:04,834 --> 02:54:13,292
"Don't think of this as farewell...
I've simply become one with you."

2118
02:54:15,751 --> 02:54:20,376
Subtitles By
Frame House Productions

